{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791709010584,"sessionID":"ses_ed5d2f61fffeMvSbVSQlxsDWfl","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_4889b9c61f194a4d9aaa7f47","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/STATE_SERVICES.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/STATE_SERVICES.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # State services\n2: \n3: Policy for the state layer: `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts`. These are the\n4: Svelte 5 runes classes that hold each domain's reactive state and own its\n5: communication with the API. Read\n6: [`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) first; this\n7: document applies those general rules to this layer.\n8: \n9: ## One class per domain, one file per domain\n10: \n11: - One exported class per domain (`Todos`, `Clipboard`, `QuickAdd`, `Auth`, …),\n12:   in one file named after it (`Todos.svelte.ts`).\n13: - `.svelte.ts` extension is required — it is what makes the runes (`$state`)\n14:   compile.\n15: - The class is the domain's single source of truth: it holds the data, exposes\n16:   the methods that change it, and is the only layer that talks to\n17:   `ApiService`. Components read it, they do not re-implement it.\n18: - No markup, no DOM, no UI strings inside the class (those belong to\n19:   components and `i18n/`).\n20: \n21: ## The context-singleton pattern\n22: \n23: Every store is a Svelte context singleton. The file exports a private `Symbol`\n24: key plus a `setX()` / `getX()` pair — the only sanctioned shape:\n25: \n26: ```ts\n27: const CLIPBOARD_KEY = Symbol('SOLYTO_CLIPBOARD');\n28: \n29: export function setClipboard(): Clipboard {\n30: \treturn setContext(CLIPBOARD_KEY, new Clipboard());\n31: }\n32: \n33: export function getClipboard(): Clipboard {\n34: \treturn getContext<Clipboard>(CLIPBOARD_KEY);\n35: }\n36: ```\n37: \n38: - `setX()` is called **once**, during component initialisation, and returns the\n39:   new instance.\n40: - `getX()` is called by any component below that needs the store. It never\n41:   constructs — a missing provider is a programming error, not a case to handle.\n42: - App-wide stores (`Auth`, `Translation`, `Viewpoint`, `KeyManager`,\n43:   `LoadingIndicator`, `UiNotifications`, `Navigation`, `CookieConsent`,\n44:   `PwaInstall`, `WelcomeTour`, `QuickAdd`) are created in\n45:   `src/routes/+layout.svelte`.\n46: - Feature stores are created in the feature's route layout — e.g.\n47:   `setTodos()`/`setTags()` in `src/routes/todos/+layout.svelte`,\n48:   `setClipboard()` in `src/routes/clipboard/+layout.svelte`,\n49:   `setBookLibrary()` in `src/routes/libraries/books/+layout.svelte`. This keeps\n50:   a feature's store alive only while its routes are mounted.\n51: \n52: ## Reactive state as `$state` class fields\n53: \n54: - Declare each piece of reactive state as a public `$state` field with an\n55:   explicit type:\n56: \n57:   ```ts\n58:   loaded = $state<boolean>(false);\n59:   todos = $state<Todo[]>([]);\n60:   activeWorkspace = $state<TodoWorkspace | null>(null);\n61:   view = $state<'list' | 'kanban' | 'overview' | 'card'>('list');\n62:   ```\n63: \n64: - Initialise to the empty/neutral value so the store is valid before `load()`\n65:   runs.\n66: - Mutate the field directly (`this.todos = res.data as Todo[]`); do not wrap it\n67:   in setters, stores or extra indirection. Svelte's runes propagate the change.\n68: - Internal-only state may be `private` (see `Viewpoint._state`), but reach for\n69:   that only when you also want to expose a stable read-only surface (next\n70:   section).\n71: \n72: ## Member ordering\n73: \n74: Keep the same order in every store, top to bottom. `Todos` is the reference:\n75: \n76: 1. `static readonly` constants (`Todos.LS_HIDE_IT_KEY`).\n77: 2. `$state` fields.\n78: 3. Collaborators/dependencies declared as typed fields (`auth`, `apiService`,\n79:    `localStorage`, injected services) and any private helpers.\n80: 4. The constructor.\n81: 5. Public methods.\n82: 6. `private` methods last.\n83: \n84: The `Symbol` key and `setX()`/`getX()` functions live **below** the class, at\n85: the bottom of the file.\n86: \n87: ## Constructor dependency injection (preferred)\n88: \n89: The preferred shape injects collaborators through constructor parameters whose\n90: defaults preserve zero-argument construction. `Todos` and `Finances` are the\n91: reference:\n92: \n93: ```ts\n94: export class Todos {\n95: \tauth: Auth;\n96: \tapiService: ApiService;\n97: \tlocalStorage: LocalStorageService;\n98: \n99: \tconstructor(\n100: \t\tauth: Auth = getAuth(),\n101: \t\tapiService: ApiService = auth.apiService,\n102: \t\tlocalStorage: LocalStorageService = new LocalStorageService()\n103: \t) {\n104: \t\tthis.auth = auth;\n105: \t\tthis.apiService = apiService;\n106: \t\tthis.localStorage = localStorage;\n107: \t}\n108: }\n109: ```\n110: \n111: ```ts\n112: export class Finances {\n113: \tauth: Auth;\n114: \tapiService: ApiService;\n115: \n116: \tconstructor(auth: Auth = getAuth(), apiService: ApiService = auth.apiService) {\n117: \t\tthis.auth = auth;\n118: \t\tthis.apiService = apiService;\n119: \t\t// …\n120: \t}\n121: }\n122: ```\n123: \n124: Why it matters:\n125: \n126: - `new Todos()` still works everywhere (the defaults do the context lookup), so\n127:   the change is invisible to callers.\n128: - Tests can pass mocks (`new Todos(mockAuth, mockApi, mockStorage)`) without\n129:   module-level `vi.mock` gymnastics — this is the refactor `docs/TESTING.md` §4\n130:   describes, and it is what made the store tests possible.\n131: - The defaults are the single place that knows how to build the real\n132:   collaborators.\n133: \n134: The **older style** some stores still use declares dependencies as\n135: field initialisers, which run before the constructor body:\n136: \n137: ```ts\n138: // older — not the target style\n139: export class Clipboard {\n140: \tauth = getAuth();\n141: \tapiService: ApiService;\n142: \n143: \tconstructor() {\n144: \t\tthis.apiService = this.auth.apiService;\n145: \t}\n146: }\n147: ```\n148: \n149: This works, but it cannot be overridden by a constructor argument and forces\n150: tests to mock the `Auth` module. When you touch a store, prefer migrating it to\n151: the injectable shape; do not do it as a bulk rewrite.\n152: \n153: The shared API client is `auth.apiService` — `Auth` owns one `ApiService`\n154: instance and keeps its token current (`updateAuthToken`). Stores default to it;\n155: do not construct a second `ApiService` with a hand-copied token.\n156: \n157: ## The `load()` + `loaded` convention\n158: \n159: Every domain store exposes an async `load(): Promise<void>` that fetches its\n160: data and populates the `$state` fields, and a boolean `loaded` field set to\n161: `true` on the first successful load. Components/layouts call `load()` in\n162: `onMount` and use `loaded` to avoid rendering empty state.\n163: \n164: ```ts\n165: async load(): Promise<void> {\n166: \tconst res = await this.apiService.list(apiRoutes.todos.list);\n167: \n168: \tif (res) {\n169: \t\tthis.loaded = true;\n170: \t\tthis.todos = res.data as Todo[];\n171: \t\tthis.filteredTodos = this.todos;\n172: \t\t// …\n173: \t}\n174: \n175: \t// … derived steps, then parallel sub-loads\n176: }\n177: ```\n178: \n179: - One `if (res)` block does the assignment; failure simply leaves the previous\n180:   state in place (see error semantics in [`DATA_LAYER.md`](DATA_LAYER.md)).\n181: - Sub-loads use their own `loadX()` methods and may run in parallel via\n182:   `Promise.all`.\n183: - `load()` re-derives everything that depends on the freshly-loaded data, so a\n184:   store is never left half-updated.\n185: \n186: ## The CRUD method pattern\n187: \n188: Every create/update/delete method follows the same shape: call `ApiService`\n189: with a route from `apiRoutes`, reload on success, return a boolean.\n190: \n191: ```ts\n192: async delete(todo: Todo): Promise<boolean> {\n193: \tconst ok = await this.apiService.delete(apiRoutes.todos.delete, todo.id);\n194: \tif (ok) await this.load();\n195: \treturn ok;\n196: }\n197: ```\n198: \n199: ```ts\n200: async addTag(todo: Todo, tagId: number): Promise<boolean> {\n201: \tconst tagIds = todo.tags.map((t) => t.id);\n202: \tconst request: UpdateTodoRequest = { tags: tagIds.concat([tagId]) };\n203: \tconst res = await this.apiService.update(apiRoutes.todos.update, todo.id, request);\n204: \tif (res) await this.load();\n205: \treturn res;\n206: }\n207: ```\n208: \n209: - Build a typed request object first (`const request: UpdateTodoRequest = {…}`),\n210:   then pass it to `ApiService`.\n211: - Return `true`/`false` (or the raw `res`/`ok`) so the calling component can\n212:   react. Mutating methods that need a created entity return it (or `null`).\n213: - **This repetitiveness is intentional.** It is not something to \"DRY up\" behind\n214:   a generic `crud(endpoint, method, id)` helper — each method is a greppable,\n215:   independently-readable contract with its own request type, and the\n216:   boilerplate CRUD wrappers are explicitly excluded from test coverage\n217:   (`docs/TESTING.md` §8). Copy the nearest method; do not abstract it.\n218: \n219: ## Delegate pure logic to `services/`\n220: \n221: A store is glue: it holds state and sequences API/pure calls. Filtering,\n222: sorting, grouping and scoring are pure and live in `src/lib/services/`:\n223: \n224: - `Todos` delegates to `TodoFilterService`, `TodoSortingService`,\n225:   `TodoGroupingService` and `TodoRelevanceService` — e.g.\n226:   `this.filteredTodos = this.filterService.filter(filter, this.filteredTodos)`.\n227: - The service instances are held as fields (`filterService = new TodoFilterService()`)\n228:   and called from the store's methods.\n229: - Library stores hold a `LibraryFilterService`; `Finances` uses\n230:   `WealthStatisticsService`.\n231: \n232: If you are about to write a non-trivial `filter`/`map`/`reduce` chain inside a\n233: store method, stop: it probably belongs in a `*Service.ts` where it can be unit\n234: tested without any Svelte context. See [`DATA_LAYER.md`](DATA_LAYER.md).\n235: \n236: ## Persistence\n237: \n238: The only client-side persistence is `LocalStorageService`, injected into the\n239: store. Storage keys are class constants named `LS_*`:\n240: \n241: ```ts\n242: export class Todos {\n243: \tstatic readonly LS_HIDE_IT_KEY: string = 'todos_hideit';\n244: \t// …\n245: }\n246: ```\n247: \n248: ```ts\n249: this.hideItActive = this.localStorage.getBool(Todos.LS_HIDE_IT_KEY) ?? false;\n250: ```\n251: \n252: - Always go through `LocalStorageService` — it guards `browser` internally, so\n253:   callers do not have to.\n254: - Keys are `snake_case` strings (`'todos_hideit'`, `'custom_api_url'`).\n255: - Restore persisted state in the constructor, and re-read it in `load()` when a\n256:   value could have changed while the initial load was in flight (see\n257:   `Todos.loadHideIt()`). Auth tokens are the one exception handled by `Auth`\n258:   itself.\n259: \n260: ## Browser and route imports — guard them\n261: \n262: - `browser` from `$app/environment` guards anything that touches `window`,\n263:   `document` or `localStorage`. `LocalStorageService` does this internally; a\n264:   store that touches the DOM directly must do the same. `Viewpoint` guards its\n265:   entire initialisation behind `if (browser)`.\n266: - `page` from `$app/state` is read for route information (e.g.\n267:   `page.url.searchParams` in `Todos.checkUrlForFilter()`). Read it; do not\n268:   subscribe to navigation inside the store.\n269: - If a store registers listeners or timers, clean them up in an explicit\n270:   `destroy()` method and call it from the owner component's `onDestroy`.\n271:   `Viewpoint` collects each cleanup closure in an array and runs them all in\n272:   `destroy()`.\n273: \n274: ## Stores may depend on other stores\n275: \n276: A store may read another store or the translation table when its logic needs\n277: them:\n278: \n279: - `QuickAdd` reads `getTranslation()` and `getUiNotifications()` for its error\n280:   messages, and `getAuth()` for the API client.\n281: - `Translation` reads `getAuth()` to pick the user's language.\n282: \n283: Resolve these dependencies once in the constructor (or as defaults), not on\n284: every method call, and never create a cycle. Keep the dependency in the\n285: constructor's parameter list where practical so tests can inject it\n286: (`docs/TESTING.md` §4 gives `QuickAdd` as the `ts`/`notifications` example).\n287: \n288: ## Read-only view state via getters\n289: \n290: When a store owns computed state that consumers must not write, expose it\n291: through getters. `Viewpoint` keeps its data in a `private _state` and returns\n292: `get state()`, `get width()`, `get isDesktop()`, etc.:\n293: \n294: ```ts\n295: private _state = $state<ViewPointState>({ width: 0, height: 0, isDesktop: false, isMobile: true, isTablet: false });\n296: \n297: get isDesktop() {\n298: \treturn this._state.isDesktop;\n299: }\n300: ```\n301: \n302: Use this for genuinely read-only derivations (screen class, computed URL\n303: flags). For normal domain data, keep the public `$state` field — getters for\n304: everything add noise.\n305: \n306: ## What not to do\n307: \n308: - **No markup, DOM, or UI strings** in a store. That is the component layer's\n309:   job.\n310: - **No hardcoded API URLs.** Every endpoint comes from\n311:   `src/lib/config/apiRoutes.ts`; never build a URL string by hand.\n312: - **No inline `fetch`.** `ApiService` is the single network seam; a store calls\n313:   it and nothing else. (The only exceptions are the few legacy direct-`fetch`\n314:   methods in `Calendars` — do not copy them.)\n315: - **No giant methods.** Split by named steps (`loadCategories`, `useFilters`).\n316: - **No new global singletons.** Use the context pattern; do not export a\n317:   module-level `new Todos()`.\n318: - **No `$derived` dumping ground.** Derived values that belong in a method or a\n319:   service stay there; see [`BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md#derived-discipline).\n320: - Do not add an abstraction a store does not already use.\n321: \n322: ## Related docs\n323: \n324: - [`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) — general in-file rules.\n325: - [`docs/DATA_LAYER.md`](DATA_LAYER.md) — `ApiService`, `apiRoutes`, services,\n326:   helpers, types, i18n.\n327: - [`docs/COMPONENTS.md`](COMPONENTS.md) — how components read these stores.\n328: - [`docs/TESTING.md`](TESTING.md) §3–4 — the store test recipe and the\n329:   constructor-injection refactor.\n\n(End of file - total 329 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# State services\n\nPolicy for the state layer: `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts`. These are the\nSvelte 5 runes classes that hold each domain's reactive state and own its\ncommunication with the API. Read\n[`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) first; this\ndocument applies those general rules to this layer.\n\n## One class per domain, one file per domain\n\n- One exported class per domain (`Todos`, `Clipboard`, `QuickAdd`, `Auth`, …),\n  in one file named after it (`Todos.svelte.ts`).\n- `.svelte.ts` extension is required — it is what makes the runes (`$state`)\n  compile.\n- The class is the domain's single source of truth: it holds the data, exposes\n  the methods that change it, and is the only layer that talks to\n  `ApiService`. Components read it, they do not re-implement it.\n- No markup, no DOM, no UI strings inside the class (those belong to\n  components and `i18n/`).\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/STATE_SERVICES.md","text":"# State services\n\nPolicy for the state layer: `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts`. These are the\nSvelte 5 runes classes that hold each domain's reactive state and own its\ncommunication with the API. Read\n[`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) first; this\ndocument applies those general rules to this layer.\n\n## One class per domain, one file per domain\n\n- One exported class per domain (`Todos`, `Clipboard`, `QuickAdd`, `Auth`, …),\n  in one file named after it (`Todos.svelte.ts`).\n- `.svelte.ts` extension is required — it is what makes the runes (`$state`)\n  compile.\n- The class is the domain's single source of truth: it holds the data, exposes\n  the methods that change it, and is the only layer that talks to\n  `ApiService`. Components read it, they do not re-implement it.\n- No markup, no DOM, no UI strings inside the class (those belong to\n  components and `i18n/`).\n\n## The context-singleton pattern\n\nEvery store is a Svelte context singleton. The file exports a private `Symbol`\nkey plus a `setX()` / `getX()` pair — the only sanctioned shape:\n\n```ts\nconst CLIPBOARD_KEY = Symbol('SOLYTO_CLIPBOARD');\n\nexport function setClipboard(): Clipboard {\n\treturn setContext(CLIPBOARD_KEY, new Clipboard());\n}\n\nexport function getClipboard(): Clipboard {\n\treturn getContext<Clipboard>(CLIPBOARD_KEY);\n}\n```\n\n- `setX()` is called **once**, during component initialisation, and returns the\n  new instance.\n- `getX()` is called by any component below that needs the store. It never\n  constructs — a missing provider is a programming error, not a case to handle.\n- App-wide stores (`Auth`, `Translation`, `Viewpoint`, `KeyManager`,\n  `LoadingIndicator`, `UiNotifications`, `Navigation`, `CookieConsent`,\n  `PwaInstall`, `WelcomeTour`, `QuickAdd`) are created in\n  `src/routes/+layout.svelte`.\n- Feature stores are created in the feature's route layout — e.g.\n  `setTodos()`/`setTags()` in `src/routes/todos/+layout.svelte`,\n  `setClipboard()` in `src/routes/clipboard/+layout.svelte`,\n  `setBookLibrary()` in `src/routes/libraries/books/+layout.svelte`. This keeps\n  a feature's store alive only while its routes are mounted.\n\n## Reactive state as `$state` class fields\n\n- Declare each piece of reactive state as a public `$state` field with an\n  explicit type:\n\n  ```ts\n  loaded = $state<boolean>(false);\n  todos = $state<Todo[]>([]);\n  activeWorkspace = $state<TodoWorkspace | null>(null);\n  view = $state<'list' | 'kanban' | 'overview' | 'card'>('list');\n  ```\n\n- Initialise to the empty/neutral value so the store is valid before `load()`\n  runs.\n- Mutate the field directly (`this.todos = res.data as Todo[]`); do not wrap it\n  in setters, stores or extra indirection. Svelte's runes propagate the change.\n- Internal-only state may be `private` (see `Viewpoint._state`), but reach for\n  that only when you also want to expose a stable read-only surface (next\n  section).\n\n## Member ordering\n\nKeep the same order in every store, top to bottom. `Todos` is the reference:\n\n1. `static readonly` constants (`Todos.LS_HIDE_IT_KEY`).\n2. `$state` fields.\n3. Collaborators/dependencies declared as typed fields (`auth`, `apiService`,\n   `localStorage`, injected services) and any private helpers.\n4. The constructor.\n5. Public methods.\n6. `private` methods last.\n\nThe `Symbol` key and `setX()`/`getX()` functions live **below** the class, at\nthe bottom of the file.\n\n## Constructor dependency injection (preferred)\n\nThe preferred shape injects collaborators through constructor parameters whose\ndefaults preserve zero-argument construction. `Todos` and `Finances` are the\nreference:\n\n```ts\nexport class Todos {\n\tauth: Auth;\n\tapiService: ApiService;\n\tlocalStorage: LocalStorageService;\n\n\tconstructor(\n\t\tauth: Auth = getAuth(),\n\t\tapiService: ApiService = auth.apiService,\n\t\tlocalStorage: LocalStorageService = new LocalStorageService()\n\t) {\n\t\tthis.auth = auth;\n\t\tthis.apiService = apiService;\n\t\tthis.localStorage = localStorage;\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n```ts\nexport class Finances {\n\tauth: Auth;\n\tapiService: ApiService;\n\n\tconstructor(auth: Auth = getAuth(), apiService: ApiService = auth.apiService) {\n\t\tthis.auth = auth;\n\t\tthis.apiService = apiService;\n\t\t// …\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nWhy it matters:\n\n- `new Todos()` still works everywhere (the defaults do the context lookup), so\n  the change is invisible to callers.\n- Tests can pass mocks (`new Todos(mockAuth, mockApi, mockStorage)`) without\n  module-level `vi.mock` gymnastics — this is the refactor `docs/TESTING.md` §4\n  describes, and it is what made the store tests possible.\n- The defaults are the single place that knows how to build the real\n  collaborators.\n\nThe **older style** some stores still use declares dependencies as\nfield initialisers, which run before the constructor body:\n\n```ts\n// older — not the target style\nexport class Clipboard {\n\tauth = getAuth();\n\tapiService: ApiService;\n\n\tconstructor() {\n\t\tthis.apiService = this.auth.apiService;\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nThis works, but it cannot be overridden by a constructor argument and forces\ntests to mock the `Auth` module. When you touch a store, prefer migrating it to\nthe injectable shape; do not do it as a bulk rewrite.\n\nThe shared API client is `auth.apiService` — `Auth` owns one `ApiService`\ninstance and keeps its token current (`updateAuthToken`). Stores default to it;\ndo not construct a second `ApiService` with a hand-copied token.\n\n## The `load()` + `loaded` convention\n\nEvery domain store exposes an async `load(): Promise<void>` that fetches its\ndata and populates the `$state` fields, and a boolean `loaded` field set to\n`true` on the first successful load. Components/layouts call `load()` in\n`onMount` and use `loaded` to avoid rendering empty state.\n\n```ts\nasync load(): Promise<void> {\n\tconst res = await this.apiService.list(apiRoutes.todos.list);\n\n\tif (res) {\n\t\tthis.loaded = true;\n\t\tthis.todos = res.data as Todo[];\n\t\tthis.filteredTodos = this.todos;\n\t\t// …\n\t}\n\n\t// … derived steps, then parallel sub-loads\n}\n```\n\n- One `if (res)` block does the assignment; failure simply leaves the previous\n  state in place (see error semantics in [`DATA_LAYER.md`](DATA_LAYER.md)).\n- Sub-loads use their own `loadX()` methods and may run in parallel via\n  `Promise.all`.\n- `load()` re-derives everything that depends on the freshly-loaded data, so a\n  store is never left half-updated.\n\n## The CRUD method pattern\n\nEvery create/update/delete method follows the same shape: call `ApiService`\nwith a route from `apiRoutes`, reload on success, return a boolean.\n\n```ts\nasync delete(todo: Todo): Promise<boolean> {\n\tconst ok = await this.apiService.delete(apiRoutes.todos.delete, todo.id);\n\tif (ok) await this.load();\n\treturn ok;\n}\n```\n\n```ts\nasync addTag(todo: Todo, tagId: number): Promise<boolean> {\n\tconst tagIds = todo.tags.map((t) => t.id);\n\tconst request: UpdateTodoRequest = { tags: tagIds.concat([tagId]) };\n\tconst res = await this.apiService.update(apiRoutes.todos.update, todo.id, request);\n\tif (res) await this.load();\n\treturn res;\n}\n```\n\n- Build a typed request object first (`const request: UpdateTodoRequest = {…}`),\n  then pass it to `ApiService`.\n- Return `true`/`false` (or the raw `res`/`ok`) so the calling component can\n  react. Mutating methods that need a created entity return it (or `null`).\n- **This repetitiveness is intentional.** It is not something to \"DRY up\" behind\n  a generic `crud(endpoint, method, id)` helper — each method is a greppable,\n  independently-readable contract with its own request type, and the\n  boilerplate CRUD wrappers are explicitly excluded from test coverage\n  (`docs/TESTING.md` §8). Copy the nearest method; do not abstract it.\n\n## Delegate pure logic to `services/`\n\nA store is glue: it holds state and sequences API/pure calls. Filtering,\nsorting, grouping and scoring are pure and live in `src/lib/services/`:\n\n- `Todos` delegates to `TodoFilterService`, `TodoSortingService`,\n  `TodoGroupingService` and `TodoRelevanceService` — e.g.\n  `this.filteredTodos = this.filterService.filter(filter, this.filteredTodos)`.\n- The service instances are held as fields (`filterService = new TodoFilterService()`)\n  and called from the store's methods.\n- Library stores hold a `LibraryFilterService`; `Finances` uses\n  `WealthStatisticsService`.\n\nIf you are about to write a non-trivial `filter`/`map`/`reduce` chain inside a\nstore method, stop: it probably belongs in a `*Service.ts` where it can be unit\ntested without any Svelte context. See [`DATA_LAYER.md`](DATA_LAYER.md).\n\n## Persistence\n\nThe only client-side persistence is `LocalStorageService`, injected into the\nstore. Storage keys are class constants named `LS_*`:\n\n```ts\nexport class Todos {\n\tstatic readonly LS_HIDE_IT_KEY: string = 'todos_hideit';\n\t// …\n}\n```\n\n```ts\nthis.hideItActive = this.localStorage.getBool(Todos.LS_HIDE_IT_KEY) ?? false;\n```\n\n- Always go through `LocalStorageService` — it guards `browser` internally, so\n  callers do not have to.\n- Keys are `snake_case` strings (`'todos_hideit'`, `'custom_api_url'`).\n- Restore persisted state in the constructor, and re-read it in `load()` when a\n  value could have changed while the initial load was in flight (see\n  `Todos.loadHideIt()`). Auth tokens are the one exception handled by `Auth`\n  itself.\n\n## Browser and route imports — guard them\n\n- `browser` from `$app/environment` guards anything that touches `window`,\n  `document` or `localStorage`. `LocalStorageService` does this internally; a\n  store that touches the DOM directly must do the same. `Viewpoint` guards its\n  entire initialisation behind `if (browser)`.\n- `page` from `$app/state` is read for route information (e.g.\n  `page.url.searchParams` in `Todos.checkUrlForFilter()`). Read it; do not\n  subscribe to navigation inside the store.\n- If a store registers listeners or timers, clean them up in an explicit\n  `destroy()` method and call it from the owner component's `onDestroy`.\n  `Viewpoint` collects each cleanup closure in an array and runs them all in\n  `destroy()`.\n\n## Stores may depend on other stores\n\nA store may read another store or the translation table when its logic needs\nthem:\n\n- `QuickAdd` reads `getTranslation()` and `getUiNotifications()` for its error\n  messages, and `getAuth()` for the API client.\n- `Translation` reads `getAuth()` to pick the user's language.\n\nResolve these dependencies once in the constructor (or as defaults), not on\nevery method call, and never create a cycle. Keep the dependency in the\nconstructor's parameter list where practical so tests can inject it\n(`docs/TESTING.md` §4 gives `QuickAdd` as the `ts`/`notifications` example).\n\n## Read-only view state via getters\n\nWhen a store owns computed state that consumers must not write, expose it\nthrough getters. `Viewpoint` keeps its data in a `private _state` and returns\n`get state()`, `get width()`, `get isDesktop()`, etc.:\n\n```ts\nprivate _state = $state<ViewPointState>({ width: 0, height: 0, isDesktop: false, isMobile: true, isTablet: false });\n\nget isDesktop() {\n\treturn this._state.isDesktop;\n}\n```\n\nUse this for genuinely read-only derivations (screen class, computed URL\nflags). For normal domain data, keep the public `$state` field — getters for\neverything add noise.\n\n## What not to do\n\n- **No markup, DOM, or UI strings** in a store. That is the component layer's\n  job.\n- **No hardcoded API URLs.** Every endpoint comes from\n  `src/lib/config/apiRoutes.ts`; never build a URL string by hand.\n- **No inline `fetch`.** `ApiService` is the single network seam; a store calls\n  it and nothing else. (The only exceptions are the few legacy direct-`fetch`\n  methods in `Calendars` — do not copy them.)\n- **No giant methods.** Split by named steps (`loadCategories`, `useFilters`).\n- **No new global singletons.** Use the context pattern; do not export a\n  module-level `new Todos()`.\n- **No `$derived` dumping ground.** Derived values that belong in a method or a\n  service stay there; see [`BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md#derived-discipline).\n- Do not add an abstraction a store does not already use.\n\n## Related docs\n\n- [`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) — general in-file rules.\n- [`docs/DATA_LAYER.md`](DATA_LAYER.md) — `ApiService`, `apiRoutes`, services,\n  helpers, types, i18n.\n- [`docs/COMPONENTS.md`](COMPONENTS.md) — how components read these stores.\n- [`docs/TESTING.md`](TESTING.md) §3–4 — the store test recipe and the\n  constructor-injection refactor.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":329,"totalLines":329,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/STATE_SERVICES.md","time":{"start":1791709010572,"end":1791709010580}},"id":"prt_12a2dda38001KcPrmKBeRf81FC","sessionID":"ses_ed5d2f61fffeMvSbVSQlxsDWfl","messageID":"msg_12a2db432001SM3EKrkR7jiJLs"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791709010727,"sessionID":"ses_ed5d2f61fffeMvSbVSQlxsDWfl","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_3f893b0895fa4e638e4d6714","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/TESTING.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/TESTING.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Test coverage plan\n2: \n3: How to build the best possible automated test coverage for the solyto frontend.\n4: \n5: Status of this document: proposal. Nothing here is implemented yet. The phases\n6: at the bottom describe the order of work; every phase that requires new\n7: dev-dependencies needs explicit approval before `npm install` (dependencies are\n8: pinned, `engine-strict=true`).\n9: \n10: ---\n11: \n12: ## 0. Implementation status\n13: \n14: Most of the plan below is now implemented. Current state (run `npm test`):\n15: \n16: - **678 tests** (53 files) across 3 Vitest projects: `unit` (node), `stores`\n17:   (node + store-mock setup), `components` (jsdom).\n18: - Coverage: `src/lib` at **~22.8% statements / ~29.2% functions / ~22.2%\n19:   lines** (up from 8.7% / 12.4%), against the whole of `src/lib` including\n20:   the 357 untested components and 37 stores. The remaining uncovered lines\n21:   cluster in the documented out-of-scope list (§8) — heavy/skip components\n22:   (echarts, TipTap, DnD, WebAuthn, electronAPI, …) and the boilerplate CRUD\n23:   stores — which is the intended \"complete enough\" state.\n24: - New devDeps (pinned): `@vitest/coverage-v8`, `jsdom`, `@testing-library/svelte`,\n25:   `@testing-library/jest-dom`, `@testing-library/user-event`, `@testing-library/dom`.\n26: - `vitest.config.ts` now uses `sveltekit()` + three projects; `tests/unit/setup/storeMocks.ts`\n27:   registers module mocks (ApiService/Auth/LocalStorageService/`$app/state`) for the\n28:   `stores` project only, so service-boundary tests keep the real implementations.\n29: - `Todos` and `Finances` state classes received a constructor-injection refactor\n30:   (auth/apiService/localStorage), defaulting to current behaviour. Other stores\n31:   are tested without source changes via the store mocks.\n32: - Component tests run in jsdom with `resolve.conditions: ['browser']` (needed so\n33:   `svelte` resolves to the client build, not SSR) and an `Element.prototype.animate`\n34:   stub in `tests/setup/component.ts` for Svelte transitions.\n35: \n36: ### Covered so far\n37: \n38: - **Pure logic (Phase 1):** `TodoGroupingService`, `TodoRelevanceService`,\n39:   `LibraryFilterService`, `WealthStatisticsService`, `TodoFilterService` gaps\n40:   (`filterCategoriesByHideIt`, `due: 'week'`), `CheckInHelper`,\n41:   `CheckInSummaryHelper`, `ColorHelper`, `FormatHelper`, `NameHelper`, full\n42:   `DateHelper` gap coverage, `NumberHelper.europeanFormat`, all `MusicTheory/*`,\n43:   `themes.ts`, `confetti.ts`.\n44: - **Service boundary (Phase 2):** `ApiService` (fetch seam — headers, `%s`/`%d`\n45:   replacement, method/body semantics, error paths), `LocalStorageService`,\n46:   `NavHelper`, `platform.ts`, `urls.ts`, `features.ts`.\n47: - **Stores (Phase 3):** `Todos`, `Finances`, `Tags`, `UserManagement`,\n48:   `TimeTracking`, `LoadingIndicator`, `CookieConsent`, `UiNotifications`,\n49:   `Calendars` (42-day grid, per-date lookups, month/week/day navigation,\n50:   view-state persistence), `Auth` (login/register/refresh/passkey,\n51:   load-from-localStorage, `isAdmin`, `shouldRefresh` threshold, public-profile\n52:   cache — in `tests/unit/auth/` because the stores project's storeMocks\n53:   replaces the Auth module), `Notes` (newest/updated/favorites, category\n54:   lookup/titles, collapsed persistence, `selectNote`, url-active check,\n55:   create guards), all 8 library stores' **filtering** (search,\n56:   genre/rating/type/location, wishlist/lent/unidentified flags,\n57:   view-pref persistence, LinkLibrary category counts), `CheckInData`\n58:   (month navigation with year wrap, `isCurrentMonth`, date-derived\n59:   `selectedDate`, scored-trackers persistence, settings merge).\n60: - **Auth-token workflow regression:** `tests/unit/auth/AuthTokenFlow.test.ts`\n61:   pins the token snapshot semantics — `new Todos()`/`new Finances()` capture\n62:   `auth.getToken()` into their `ApiService` at construction (and send it as a\n63:   Bearer header), guarding the store-construction ordering workflow described\n64:   in §0's Docker note's sibling docs.\n65: - **Components (Phase 4a):** forms (`Checkbox`, `TextInput`, `Toggle`, `Select`),\n66:   ui primitives (`Heading`, `Badge`, `CloseButton`, `DeleteButton`, `AddButton`,\n67:   `ViewSwitcher`), `todos/Counter`, and logic leaves (`AverageNumber`, `Rating`,\n68:   `StatisticWidget`).\n69: - **Context harness (§4.3):** `tests/components/helpers/context.ts` +\n70:   `ContextHarness.svelte` seed `setTranslation`, `setKeyManager`, `setTodos`,\n71:   `setAuth`, `setLoadingIndicator`, `setUiNotifications`, `setViewPoint`,\n72:   `setCookieConsent` before rendering — unlocks the context-coupled component\n73:   tests below. `tests/setup/component.ts` additionally stubs\n74:   `Element.prototype.animate` (completing `onfinish`), `matchMedia` and the\n75:   `$env/dynamic/public` virtual module.\n76: - **Components (Phase 4b/4c):** dashboard widgets (`DueTodosWidget`,\n77:   `ScoredTodosWidget`, `EventsTodayWidget`, `UpcomingEventsWidget`,\n78:   `NewestNotesWidget`, `NewestLinksWidget`, `BookReleasesWidget`,\n79:   `MovieReleasesWidget`, `MusicReleasesWidget`, `QuoteWidget`), logic-bearing\n80:   leaves (`forms/InputAutocomplete`, `forms/InlineAutocomplete`, `forms/Slider`,\n81:   `todos/NoTodos`, `check-in/DailyCheckInIcon` + `check-in/overview/CheckInIcon`,\n82:   `libraries/shared/GenreFlexList`, `tags/TagFlexList`,\n83:   `libraries/shared/CoverImage`), and translation-only components\n84:   (  `PasswordInput`, `PasswordStrengthIndicator`, `PasswordMatchIndicator`,\n85:   `ui/CookieBanner`, `NavLegalEntry`, `PopupConfirmationModal`,\n86:   `BottomSheetConfirmationModal`, `ImportButton` + 8 provider variants:\n87:   Goodreads/Hardcover/Bgg/Steam/Deezer/Discogs/Imdb/Chefkoch).\n88: - **Secondary stores (TASK-11):** `Feeds` (loadMore pagination/recursion,\n89:   filter, library flags, subscribe duplicates), `Contacts` (`contactsAZ`\n90:   grouping/sorting/hidden books, search, photo batching), `Navigation`\n91:   (usage tracking, `promoteMobileItem` least-used swap), `QuickAdd`\n92:   (detect/auto-confirm/error branches, `isUrl`), `UserNotifications`\n93:   (unread, mark-all-read, polling with fake timers), `WelcomeTour` (step\n94:   building, navigation), `Theme` (load/apply/persist, dark-mode listener,\n95:   `patchAnimate` — with document/window/Element stubs), `PwaInstall`\n96:   (capture/install flow, iOS detection).\n97: \n98: ### Not yet covered\n99: \n100: The refined next-steps roadmap (§8, Priority 1–3 and the execution order) is\n101: now implemented: state stores with real business logic (including the\n102: secondary stores `Feeds`, `Contacts`, `Navigation`, `QuickAdd`,\n103: `UserNotifications`, `WelcomeTour`, `Theme`, `PwaInstall`), the context\n104: harness, dashboard widgets, logic-bearing leaves and the translation-only\n105: components. What remains untested is deliberately out of scope (see §8): the\n106: heavy/skip component list (§4d — echarts, TipTap/ProseMirror, DnD,\n107: svelte-gestures, WebAuthn, electronAPI, clipboard API, canvas), render-only\n108: components, and the remaining boilerplate CRUD store wrappers (`Clipboard`,\n109: `DevRequests`, `Friends`, `LibraryNavigation`, `Shortcuts`, `Statistics`,\n110: `Weather`). E2E (Phase 5) is deliberately out of scope for now — see §8.\n111: \n112: ### Docker decision\n113: \n114: The frontend does **not** get an API-style test image. The backend's one-shot\n115: `test` container exists because PHP needs `pcov` and only ever runs in Docker;\n116: the frontend test suite is 100% in-process (mocked fetch), so a test container\n117: would add orchestration with zero isolation — and the compose bind-mount of\n118: `../app/:/app` means a test container runs the host's `node_modules` anyway.\n119: Frontend tests run on the host via Vitest. Docker only enters at the future\n120: integration/E2E layer, which needs the full stack up (api/nginx at `:8000`).\n121: \n122: ---\n123: \n124: ## 1. Current state\n125: \n126: - Vitest 4.1.8 with `environment: 'node'`, `env: { TZ: 'UTC' }`, `$lib` alias,\n127:   `include: ['tests/**/*.test.ts']`.\n128: - 74 passing tests in 4 files, all **pure functions**:\n129:     - `tests/helpers/DateHelper.test.ts`, `tests/helpers/NumberHelper.test.ts`\n130:     - `tests/services/TodoFilterService.test.ts`, `tests/services/TodoSortingService.test.ts`\n131: - No component tests, no state-store tests, no E2E tests. `@testing-library/svelte`,\n132:   `jsdom`/`happy-dom`, Playwright, and coverage tooling are not installed.\n133: \n134: ### Two blockers that gate everything (empirically verified)\n135: \n136: 1. **`.svelte.ts` files cannot be imported in the current Vitest config.**\n137:    Importing any `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts` throws `ReferenceError: $state is\n138: not defined`, because the Svelte compiler plugin is not active in Vitest.\n139:    Verified with a throwaway test against `LoadingIndicator.svelte.ts`.\n140: 2. **`$app/*` and `$env/*` modules are unresolvable** (no SvelteKit aliases),\n141:    unless each test `vi.mock`s them. `$env/dynamic/public` is imported at\n142:    module load by `src/lib/config/platform.ts`, so it blocks everything\n143:    transitively (e.g. `apiRoutes.ts`).\n144: \n145: Verified working recipe: adding `@sveltejs/vite-plugin-svelte` to the Vitest\n146: config compiles runes in `.svelte.ts`, and `vi.mock`ing `$app/state`,\n147: `$app/environment`, `$env/dynamic/public`, `$lib/state/Auth.svelte`,\n148: `$lib/services/ApiService`, and `$lib/services/LocalStorageService` lets the\n149: state classes be instantiated and tested in node. (Confirmed: `new Todos()`\n150: works under that recipe.)\n151: \n152: ### Architecture facts that shape the strategy\n153: \n154: - **Pure client-side-rendered SPA.** There are zero `load` functions, no\n155:   `+server.ts`, no `+page.ts`/`+layout.ts`, no `hooks.server.ts`, no\n156:   `*.server.*` files anywhere in `src/routes`. All data is fetched in\n157:   `onMount` handlers that call `.load()` on state stores.\n158: - **Data flow:** component → state store (`src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts`) →\n159:   `ApiService` (`src/lib/services/ApiService.ts`) → REST API at\n160:   `${getApiUrl()}/api/v1` (`http://localhost:8000` in dev). `ApiService` is a\n161:   single fetch choke point — one seam to stub for the entire app.\n162: - **Stores are Svelte-context singletons:** 37 runes classes, created in\n163:   `src/routes/+layout.svelte` via `setX()`, read back via `getX()`.\n164:     - 29 of 37 call `getAuth()` at **class-field initialisation** (so even\n165:       `new X()` fails without a mocked Auth module or injected auth).\n166:     - 28 construct `new ApiService(...)` internally; 12 construct\n167:       `new LocalStorageService()`; 8 construct `new LibraryFilterService()`.\n168:     - 5 use `page` from `$app/state` (CheckInData, Finances, LibraryNavigation,\n169:       Notes, Todos); 3 use `browser` from `$app/environment`.\n170:     - `QuickAdd` additionally reads `getTranslation()` and `getUiNotifications()`.\n171: - **No DI anywhere:** stores build their own services in the constructor.\n172:   Field initializers run _before_ the constructor body, so adding constructor\n173:   parameters alone is not enough — the initializer must move into the\n174:   constructor (see §4).\n175: - **Service worker** (`src/service-worker.ts`) precaches the app shell and\n176:   uses stale-while-revalidate, but explicitly skips `/api` GETs. It does not\n177:   affect API mocking; it can serve stale shell during E2E runs and should be\n178:   blocked/cleared there.\n179: - The only type modules with runtime values are `src/lib/types/check_in.ts`\n180:   and `src/lib/types/quick_add.ts`; all other type files are erased at compile\n181:   time.\n182: \n183: ---\n184: \n185: ## 2. Strategy: a four-layer test pyramid\n186: \n187: The most coverage per effort, in order:\n188: \n189: ```\n190:                ┌─────────────┐\n191:                │  E2E (later)│  Playwright, mocked API — a few happy paths\n192:                └─────────────┘\n193:             ┌─────────────────────┐\n194:             │ Component (jsdom)   │  @testing-library/svelte — pure leaves,\n195:             │  + integration      │  then context-harnessed feature tests\n196:             └─────────────────────┘\n197:          ┌────────────────────────────┐\n198:          │  Unit: state stores        │  node + module mocks (+ small DI refactor)\n199:          └────────────────────────────┘\n200:       ┌───────────────────────────────────┐\n201:       │  Unit: pure logic (helpers,       │  node — biggest cheap win\n202:       │  services, config, ApiService)    │\n203:       └───────────────────────────────────┘\n204: ```\n205: \n206: Layer 1 and the pure part of layer 2 require **no new dependencies** (except a\n207: coverage reporter). Layers 2–4 require the infrastructure changes in §3.\n208: \n209: ---\n210: \n211: ## 3. Required infrastructure changes (enable first)\n212: \n213: ### 3.1 Fix the Vitest config (`vitest.config.ts`)\n214: \n215: Add the Svelte compiler plugin so `.svelte.ts` and `.svelte` files compile:\n216: \n217: ```ts\n218: import { sveltekit } from '@sveltejs/kit/vite';\n219: import { defineConfig } from 'vitest/config';\n220: \n221: export default defineConfig({\n222: \tplugins: [sveltekit()],\n223: \tresolve: { alias: { $lib: resolve('./src/lib') } },\n224: \ttest: {\n225: \t\tinclude: ['tests/**/*.test.ts'],\n226: \t\tenvironment: 'node',\n227: \t\tenv: { TZ: 'UTC' }\n228: \t}\n229: });\n230: ```\n231: \n232: - `sveltekit()` is the documented SvelteKit approach: it activates the Svelte\n233:   plugin (fixes `$state` in `.svelte.ts`) **and** makes `$app/*`/`$env/*`\n234:   resolvable, so most tests won't need to mock those.\n235: - Alternative if `sveltekit()` proves problematic in Vitest: use\n236:   `svelte({ compilerOptions: { runes: true } })` and `vi.mock` each `$app/*`\n237:   / `$env/*` module per test (verified working).\n238: - `$app/environment`'s `browser` flag may report `false` under node/jsdom\n239:   depending on the SvelteKit version — tests that need `browser === true`\n240:   (e.g. `LocalStorageService`) should force it:\n241:   `vi.mock('$app/environment', () => ({ browser: true, dev: true }))`.\n242: \n243: ### 3.2 Add a jsdom project for component tests\n244: \n245: Vitest 4 supports `projects`. Add a second project so the existing node tests\n246: stay untouched:\n247: \n248: ```ts\n249: test: {\n250: \tprojects: [\n251: \t\t{ test: { include: ['tests/**/*.test.ts'], environment: 'node' } },\n252: \t\t{\n253: \t\t\tplugins: [sveltekit()],\n254: \t\t\ttest: {\n255: \t\t\t\tinclude: ['tests/components/**/*.test.ts'],\n256: \t\t\t\tenvironment: 'jsdom',\n257: \t\t\t\tsetupFiles: ['tests/setup/component.ts']\n258: \t\t\t}\n259: \t\t}\n260: \t];\n261: }\n262: ```\n263: \n264: Component tests live under `tests/components/` and run in jsdom.\n265: \n266: ### 3.3 New dev-dependencies (all require approval before install)\n267: \n268: | Package                       | Purpose                                  | Version notes         |\n269: | ----------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- | --------------------- |\n270: | `@vitest/coverage-v8`         | `--coverage` reporting to drive the plan | match vitest 4.x      |\n271: | `jsdom`                       | DOM for component tests                  | latest                |\n272: | `@testing-library/svelte`     | render Svelte 5 components               | v5+ supports Svelte 5 |\n273: | `@testing-library/jest-dom`   | DOM matchers (`toBeInTheDocument`, ...)  | v6                    |\n274: | `@testing-library/user-event` | realistic clicks/typing                  | v14                   |\n275: | _(later)_ `@playwright/test`  | E2E layer                                | optional, phase 5     |\n276: \n277: ### 3.4 Test support code (`tests/` layout)\n278: \n279: ```\n280: tests/\n281:   setup/component.ts        # jest-dom import, localStorage/global stubs, cleanup\n282:   helpers/\n283:     factories.ts            # todo(), category(), tag(), checkIn() builders\n284:     context.ts              # renderWithContext(component, { stores }) — see §4.3\n285:     fetchMock.ts            # mockFetch(routes) + ApiService fake\n286:     localStorageMock.ts     # in-memory localStorage\n287:   unit/                     # node env: helpers, services, config, stores\n288:   components/               # jsdom env: component tests\n289: ```\n290: \n291: ---\n292: \n293: ## 4. Making the state layer testable (small refactor, big payoff)\n294: \n295: The stores hold most of the app's real logic (`Todos.useFilters`,\n296: `Todos.groupByStatus`, `Finances.getWealthSum`, library search/filter, ...) and\n297: are currently untestable because services are constructed internally and `auth`\n298: is a context read at field-init. The minimal, mechanical refactor:\n299: \n300: ```ts\n301: // before — field initializer runs before the constructor body\n302: export class Todos {\n303: \tauth = getAuth();\n304: \tapiService: ApiService;\n305: \tlocalStorage = new LocalStorageService();\n306: \tconstructor() {\n307: \t\tthis.apiService = new ApiService(this.auth.getToken());\n308: \t}\n309: }\n310: \n311: // after — everything injectable, defaults preserve current behaviour\n312: export class Todos {\n313: \tauth: Auth;\n314: \tapiService: ApiService;\n315: \tlocalStorage: LocalStorageService;\n316: \tconstructor(\n317: \t\tauth: Auth = getAuth(),\n318: \t\tapiService: ApiService = new ApiService(auth.getToken()),\n319: \t\tlocalStorage: LocalStorageService = new LocalStorageService()\n320: \t) {\n321: \t\tthis.auth = auth;\n322: \t\tthis.apiService = apiService;\n323: \t\tthis.localStorage = localStorage;\n324: \t}\n325: }\n326: ```\n327: \n328: This applies to:\n329: \n330: - **28 stores** constructing `ApiService`: pass it in (Auth, Todos, Notes,\n331:   Calendars, Finances, Feeds, all 8 libraries, Contacts, CheckInData,\n332:   Clipboard, DevRequests, Friends, Shortcuts, Statistics, Tags, TimeTracking,\n333:   UserManagement, UserNotifications, Weather, Navigation, QuickAdd).\n334: - **12 stores** constructing `LocalStorageService` (incl. Auth, Theme,\n335:   CookieConsent).\n336: - **8 library stores** constructing `LibraryFilterService`.\n337: - **QuickAdd**: inject `ts`/`notifications` as well.\n338: - **Stores using `page` from `$app/state`**: keep reading `page` for now and\n339:   `vi.mock('$app/state')` in tests; or inject a `getPathname`/`page` for the\n340:   cleanest seams (only 5 stores; the constructor only reads path params, not a\n341:   live value).\n342: \n343: Scope guard: this refactor is mechanical and does not change behaviour. Do it\n344: only as far as tests need it (one store at a time), not as a bulk rewrite.\n345: \n346: ### 4.1 Standard unit-test recipe for a store\n347: \n348: ```ts\n349: vi.mock('$app/state', () => ({ page: { url: new URL('http://localhost/todos') } }));\n350: vi.mock('$lib/state/Auth.svelte', () => ({\n351:   getAuth: () => ({ getToken: () => 'test-token', /* …used methods */ })\n352: }));\n353: vi.mock('$lib/services/ApiService', () => ({\n354:   default: class FakeApi {\n355:     list = vi.fn(); get = vi.fn(); create = vi.fn();\n356:     update = vi.fn(); delete = vi.fn(); post = vi.fn(); put = vi.fn();\n357:   }\n358: }));\n359: \n360: const api = new (await import('$lib/services/ApiService')).default();\n361: const store = new Todos(/* mocked auth */, api as any, /* fake storage */);\n362: \n363: // test pure logic: set store.todos, call useFilters(), assert store.filteredTodos\n364: // test CRUD: api.list.mockResolvedValue({ data: [...] }); await store.load();\n365: ```\n366: \n367: Mock only the methods a given test exercises; `ApiService` methods return\n368: `null` by default (safe no-ops) unless stubbed.\n369: \n370: ### 4.2 Priority stores to test first (highest logic density)\n371: \n372: | Store                                                                                                                         | What to cover                                                                                                                                                                         |\n373: | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n374: | `Todos.svelte.ts`                                                                                                             | `useFilters` (backlog/hide-it/category/tag/auto-generated visibility), `groupByStatus`, `checkUrlForFilter`, `quickCreate` recurrence-ignore logic, `toggleSortByScore`, `loadHideIt` |\n375: | `Finances.svelte.ts`                                                                                                          | `getWealthSum`, `getBudgetTotal`, `getBudgetIncomeTotal`, `getBudgetExpenseTotal`, `getActivePage`, `loadIncome` income/expense split                                                 |\n376: | `Auth.svelte.ts`                                                                                                              | token refresh flow, `isAdmin`, login/register request bodies, persistence keys                                                                                                        |\n377: | `Calendars.svelte.ts`                                                                                                         | `loadMonth` date math, `getEventsForDate`, view state (skip the 3 direct `fetch` methods or stub global fetch)                                                                        |\n378: | Library stores (BookLibrary, MusicLibrary, MovieLibrary, GameLibrary, PlantLibrary, QuoteLibrary, RecipeLibrary, LinkLibrary) | search/filter by genre/rating/type/location, wishlist/lent/unidentified flags, per-type `*View` prefs from localStorage                                                               |\n379: | `Notes.svelte.ts`                                                                                                             | `getNewestNotes`, `getCategoryTitle`, create/delete (mock `$app/navigation`/`$app/paths`)                                                                                             |\n380: | `CheckInData.svelte.ts`, `TimeTracking.svelte.ts`, `UserManagement.svelte.ts`, `Tags.svelte.ts`                               | pure helpers (`formatDuration`, `filterUsers`, `sort`)                                                                                                                                |\n381: \n382: ### 4.3 Component test harness (context wrapper)\n383: \n384: Because components pull stores via `getX()`, provide a render helper that\n385: seeds context before rendering:\n386: \n387: ```ts\n388: import { render } from '@testing-library/svelte';\n389: \n390: export function renderWithContext(Component, props, stores = {}) {\n391: \t// wrapper component:\n392: \t//   setTranslation(mockTs); setKeyManager(mock); setTodos(mockTodos);\n393: \t//   setAuth(mockAuth); setLoadingIndicator(mock); setUiNotifications(mock);\n394: \t//   <Component {...props} />\n395: \t// store mocks = real store instances with apiService stubbed, or `vi.mock`ed modules\n396: }\n397: ```\n398: \n399: Build the wrapper once with the six most common stores (`Translation`,\n400: `KeyManager`, `Todos`, `Auth`, `LoadingIndicator`, `UiNotifications`) —\n401: unlocks ~250 context-coupled components.\n402: \n403: ---\n404: \n405: ## 5. Coverage roadmap (layered, in order)\n406: \n407: ### Phase 1 — Complete pure-logic unit tests (node, no new deps) ✅ high ROI\n408: \n409: Finish the untested pure modules. Current gaps:\n410: \n411: **Services**\n412: \n413: - `TodoGroupingService` — `groupByStatus` (untested, pure).\n414: - `TodoRelevanceService` — `getScoredTodos` (pure, uses `daysSince`; use fake timers/fixed date).\n415: - `LibraryFilterService` — `search`, `byRating`, `byGenre`, `byGenreAndRating`, `byType`, `byLocation`, `byUnidentified`, `byWishlist`, `byLent` (pure, type-only imports).\n416: - `WealthStatisticsService` — `getGraphValues` (pure; `SvelteDate` + `getUrlFormat`; fix the \"current date\" with fake timers).\n417: - `TodoFilterService` gaps — `filterCategoriesByHideIt`, `due: 'week'` case.\n418: \n419: **Helpers**\n420: \n421: - `CheckInHelper` — `getMeanValue`, `getTotalMeanValue`.\n422: - `CheckInSummaryHelper` — `buildDaySummary`, `buildPeriodSummary`, `getDayLabel`.\n423: - `ColorHelper` — `lightenColor`.\n424: - `FormatHelper` — `nl2br`, `markdownToHtml` (uses `marked`, node-safe).\n425: - `NameHelper` — `getInitials`.\n426: - `MusicTheoryHelper` + all 4 `MusicTheory/*` modules (ChordGenerator, NoteOperations, ScaleGenerator, TheoryConstants) — large pure surface, snapshot the constants.\n427: - `DateHelper` gaps (~14 functions): `formatDateWithWeekday`, `formatFloatingDate`, `getUrlFormat`, `getDaysInMonth`, `getLast30Days`, `getNextXDays`, `isDateThisWeek`, `isDateLast7Days`, `getCurrentTimestamp`, `getCurrentYearMonthString`, `getISODateInfo`, `getCalendarMonth`, `getCalendarWeek`, `dateFromTimestamp`.\n428: - `NumberHelper` gap — `europeanFormat`.\n429: \n430: **Config / effects**\n431: \n432: - `themes.ts` — pure data.\n433: - `effects/confetti.ts` — `createConfettiOptions` merges options (type-only import, pure).\n434: \n435: ### Phase 2 — Service boundary tests (node, tiny mocks)\n436: \n437: - `ApiService` — stub `globalThis.fetch` (`vi.stubGlobal`): assert `list/get/create/delete/update/post/put/postFormData/uploadFile` send the right method, URL (`%s`/`%d` replacement), headers (Bearer token present/absent, Content-Type for bodies), and return semantics on `ok`/error. This is the single most valuable test target — it is the only network seam.\n438: - `LocalStorageService` — `vi.mock('$app/environment', () => ({ browser: true }))` + in-memory `localStorage` stub; assert get/set/getJson/getNumber/getBool/destroy round-trips and JSON parse-failure → null.\n439: - `NavHelper` — `vi.mock('$app/state')`; cover `getPageSlug`, `getPageFeature`, `showNavbar`, `isDashboard`, `isAdminRoute`, `isAuthRoute`, `isSetupRoute`.\n440: - `platform.ts` / `urls.ts` / `features.ts` / `navigation.ts` / `apiRoutes.ts` — `vi.mock('$env/dynamic/public')` + `$app/*` + `localStorage`; assert `getApiUrl` resolution order (env → hostname map → fallback), custom-API URL persistence, `PLATFORM`/`IS_NATIVE` flags. Use `vi.resetModules()` + fresh `$env` mocks for isolation.\n441: \n442: ### Phase 3 — State stores (node + module mocks, after §4 refactor)\n443: \n444: Apply the §4.1 recipe. Full inventory by group (37 files):\n445: \n446: | Group            | Stores                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | Extra mocks needed                                                                                                                             |\n447: | ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n448: | Root             | `Auth`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | `$env/dynamic/public`, ApiService, LocalStorageService                                                                                         |\n449: | No-auth (8)      | `LoadingIndicator`, `UiNotifications`, `WelcomeTour`, `PwaInstall`, `Viewpoint`, `CookieConsent`, `Theme`, `LibraryNavigation`                                                                                                                                                                                                           | `LoadingIndicator` testable as-is; `WelcomeTour`/`LibraryNavigation` need `urls`/`$app/state` mocks; `Theme` DOM methods need jsdom or adapter |\n450: | Auth+CRUD (21)   | `Todos`, `Notes`, `Calendars`, `Finances`, `Feeds`, `Contacts`, `BookLibrary`, `MusicLibrary`, `MovieLibrary`, `GameLibrary`, `PlantLibrary`, `QuoteLibrary`, `RecipeLibrary`, `LinkLibrary`, `Clipboard`, `DevRequests`, `Friends`, `Shortcuts`, `Statistics`, `Tags`, `TimeTracking`, `UserManagement`, `UserNotifications`, `Weather` | Auth + ApiService (+ LocalStorageService for the 12 that use it)                                                                               |\n451: | `page` users (5) | CheckInData, Finances, LibraryNavigation, Notes, Todos                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | `$app/state`                                                                                                                                   |\n452: | Special          | `QuickAdd` (3 contexts), `Navigation` (`$env/dynamic/public` + `auth.user.settings`), `Translation` (`browser` + `navigator.language`)                                                                                                                                                                                                   | per-file                                                                                                                                       |\n453: \n454: ### Phase 4 — Component tests (jsdom, after §3.2/§3.3)\n455: \n456: **4a. Pure/presentational leaves (~70, low effort).** No context, no `$app`:\n457: \n458: - `forms/` (11): Checkbox, DateInput, DateTimeInput, NumberInput, TextInput, Select, Slider, Toggle, SvelteDateInput, InputAutocomplete, InlineAutocomplete.\n459: - `ui/buttons/` (17): AcceptButton, AddButton, CloseButton, CloudButton, DeleteButton, EditButton, FunnelButton, HamburgerButton, IconButton, ImportButton, InlineDeleteButton, InlineEditButton, InlineExpandButton, RefreshButton, SaveButton, StarButton, TextButton.\n460: - `ui/icons/` (12), `ui/menus/` (2: MenuIcon, RightClickMenu), `ui/` primitives (~18): Badge, Card, Divider, File, Flag, Heading, SubHeading, ModalFormRow, Tabs, ViewSwitcher, NavEntry, NavEntryIcon, MovableHoverBox, HelpTooltip, LoadingLogo, StaggeredLogo, QuickSelectOverlay, PopupContentModal, BottomSheetModal, SlidingSideBar.\n461: - Feature leaves: `todos/Counter`, `check-in/` (DailyCheckInIcon, CheckInIcon, AverageNumber), `libraries/shared/` (Rating, CoverImage, MissingCover, GenreFlexList, ExternalSearchLink, BookRelease), `tags/TagFlexList`, `dev-requests/Author`, `guitar/GuitarTheoryNavigation`, `admin/StatisticWidget`, `notes/AddFolderButton`/`AddNoteButton`/`editor/ToolbarDivider`, `settings/SettingsSection` + SettingsNavigation*, `dashboard/widgets/*` (the props-driven ones: DueTodosWidget, ScoredTodosWidget, EventsTodayWidget, UpcomingEventsWidget, NewestNotesWidget, NewestLinksWidget, BookReleasesWidget, MovieReleasesWidget, MusicReleasesWidget, QuoteWidget).\n462: \n463: **4b. Translation-only components (~20).** Presentational but call `getTranslation()`; become trivial once the §4.3 harness exists: the `*ImportButton`/`*Button` icons, `NoTodos`, `PasswordInput`, `PasswordStrengthIndicator`, `PasswordMatchIndicator`, `ui/CookieBanner`, `PopupConfirmationModal`, `BottomSheetConfirmationModal`, `NavLegalEntry`.\n464: \n465: **4c. KeyManager + domain integration.** With `setKeyManager()`/`setTodos()`/`setAuth()`/`setLoadingIndicator()`/`setUiNotifications()`/`setViewPoint()` in the harness:\n466: \n467: - Todos feature: `views/{CardView,ListView,OverviewView}`, `props/*` (Category, DueDate, Effort, Flags, Link, Priority, Progress, Recurrence, Status, Subtasks, Tags, Title), `actions/{TodoCreate,TodoDelete,HideIt,SortByScore}`, `TodoNavigation*`, `ListAndAdd`.\n468: - Calendars: `views/{day,week,month,list}/*`, `NavigationEntry`, `MobileCalendarHeader`.\n469: - Dashboard: `YourDay`, `QuickGlance`, plus context widgets.\n470: - Libraries: shared `Entries/Header/Search/ShelfView/SpineView/CreateModal/DetailModal`.\n471: - Feeds, time-tracking, notes, check-in, settings, finances as capacity allows.\n472: \n473: **4d. Heavy/skip (~15 components).** Do not attempt in jsdom without heavy stubbing — exclude from automated coverage or stub their leaf dependencies:\n474: `charts/*` (echarts), `notes/editor/*` (TipTap/ProseMirror), `todos/views/KanbanView` (svelte-dnd-action), `ui/Notifications` (svelte-gestures), `settings/SecuritySettings` (simplewebauthn), `forms/{DatePicker,MultiSelect}` (datepicker/svelte-multiselect), `settings/{TagEdit,LocalizationSettings}`, `contacts/AddressBook*` (color picker, tzdb), dompurify/marked-rich components, `desktop/TitleBar` + `settings/UpdateChecker` (electronAPI), `clipboard/ClipboardList` (clipboard API), `tour/WelcomeTour`, `quick-add/QuickAddModal`. `ImageService.resizeImage` (canvas) is likewise skipped or reduced to pure resize-math.\n475: \n476: ### Phase 5 — E2E (optional, later)\n477: \n478: If desired, Playwright against the real dev server with API responses mocked at\n479: `http://localhost:8000/api/v1/**` (or via a stub server). High-value flows:\n480: auth (email/password + WebAuthn virtual authenticator), todos CRUD, calendar\n481: month navigation, a library search. Must block/clear the service-worker cache\n482: (`serviceWorkers: 'block'` or `caches.delete()`) for deterministic runs.\n483: \n484: ---\n485: \n486: ## 6. Expected coverage & measurement\n487: \n488: - Use `@vitest/coverage-v8` with `npm run test:coverage`.\n489: - Treat coverage as a **signal, not a target**: after the §8 roadmap, the\n490:   remaining uncovered code should be the explicit out-of-scope list — third-party\n491:   wrappers, canvas/DOM-heavy leaves, and render-only components.\n492: - Keep the out-of-scope paths excluded (`exclude` in the coverage config) so\n493:   the number stays honest and comparable over time.\n494: - Re-measure after each priority and watch _where_ the uncovered lines are,\n495:   not the headline percentage. The number will stay modest while the 357\n496:   components and 37 stores exist, because most of them are intentionally not\n497:   tested (see §8).\n498: \n499: ## 7. Risks & caveats\n500: \n501: - **SvelteKit `$app/state` `page` object** in tests is a static mock; code that\n502:   reacts to `page` changes won't be exercised at unit level (fine — component\n503:   tests cover rendering paths).\n504: - **Run/effect timing:** stores use `setTimeout`/`tick`/`setInterval`\n505:   (`quickCreate`, `recentlyCreated`, `UserNotifications`, `Calendars`,\n506:   `Notes`). Use `vi.useFakeTimers()` and `flushSync`/`await tick()`.\n507: - **`SvelteDate` ignores `vi.setSystemTime`:** `svelte/reactivity`'s `SvelteDate`\n508:   captures the native `Date` at module load (in both the client and server\n509:   builds), so the fake-timer clock never reaches `new SvelteDate()` — it always\n510:   returns the real current time. Tests that exercise store code reading \"now\"\n511:   via `SvelteDate` (`Calendars` constructor/`goToToday`, `CheckInData`\n512:   initialisation/`isCurrentMonth`) must therefore assert against the real\n513:   `new Date()` on real timers, never against a hardcoded date — a hardcoded\n514:   \"today\" only passes on the day it was written.\n515: - **jsdom gaps:** `matchMedia`, `ResizeObserver`, `IntersectionObserver`,\n516:   `navigator.clipboard`, canvas 2D context need small stubs in\n517:   `tests/setup/component.ts`.\n518: - **i18n invariant:** when adding/verifying UI strings in component tests,\n519:   keep all four locales (`en/de/es/fr`) in sync — `npm run check` enforces it.\n520: - **Pinned deps:** all additions must be pinned and installed only with\n521:   approval (AGENTS.md hard rule).\n522: - **Do not over-test third-party wrappers:** ECharts/TipTap/DnD behavior is the\n523:   library's responsibility; assert our props/logic, not their internals.\n524: \n525: ## 8. Next steps — where to invest next (current roadmap)\n526: \n527: Guiding rule: **test what has logic or a contract worth pinning; nothing else.**\n528: The 8.7% figure is low because the denominator is the whole of `src/lib` (357\n529: components, 37 stores), most of which is boilerplate or third-party wrappers.\n530: Raise it by testing the real logic — not by chasing a number.\n531: \n532: ### Priority 1 — State stores with real business logic (highest value)\n533: \n534: | Store                  | What is genuinely testable                                                                                                                                                                         |\n535: | ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n536: | `Calendars`            | `loadMonth` (42-day grid math), `getEventsForDate`, month/week/day navigation, view state                                                                                                          |\n537: | `Auth`                 | login/register/refresh/passkey flows, load-from-localStorage, token-expiry branch, `isAdmin` — the security surface; the token-capture recipe is proven in `tests/unit/auth/AuthTokenFlow.test.ts` |\n538: | `Notes`                | `getNewestNotes`, `getCategoryTitle`, create/delete (mock `$app/navigation`/`$app/paths`)                                                                                                          |\n539: | Library stores (all 8) | the **non-CRUD** parts: search/filter by genre/rating/type/location, wishlist/lent/unidentified flags, view-pref persistence                                                                       |\n540: | `CheckInData`          | month navigation, date-derived `selectedDate`, scoring                                                                                                                                             |\n541: \n542: Do **not** test the ~20 boilerplate CRUD wrappers (`createX`/`updateX`/`deleteX`\n543: = call the API + reload). Prove the pattern once per store, then move on.\n544: \n545: ### Priority 2 — Presentational components _with logic_\n546: \n547: Most of the ~70 \"pure\" leaves (icons, logos, dividers) are render-only and not\n548: worth tests. Real value is in:\n549: \n550: - Keyboard/selection logic: `forms/InputAutocomplete`, `forms/InlineAutocomplete`,\n551:   `forms/Slider`.\n552: - State-driven leaves: `todos/NoTodos`, `check-in/DailyCheckInIcon`/`CheckInIcon`,\n553:   `libraries/shared/GenreFlexList`, `tags/TagFlexList`, `libraries/shared/CoverImage`.\n554: - Props-driven dashboard widgets (`DueTodosWidget`, `ScoredTodosWidget`,\n555:   `UpcomingEventsWidget`, …) — data + handlers come in as props, making them the\n556:   cleanest integration targets in the app.\n557: - Translation-only components (~20 `*ImportButton`s, `NoTodos`, password\n558:   indicators) — only after Priority 3's harness exists.\n559: \n560: ### Priority 3 — Context harness (enabling investment)\n561: \n562: One `renderWithContext` helper that seeds `setTranslation()`, `setKeyManager()`,\n563: `setTodos()`, `setAuth()`, `setLoadingIndicator()`, `setUiNotifications()`,\n564: `setViewPoint()` before rendering (pattern in §4.3). This unlocks the ~250\n565: context-coupled components (todos views/props/actions, calendar views, dashboard)\n566: and the translation-only leaves. Without it, the mock boilerplate per component\n567: test is not worth the effort.\n568: \n569: ### Explicitly out of scope\n570: \n571: - Heavy/skip list (§4d): echarts, TipTap/ProseMirror, DnD (`KanbanView`),\n572:   svelte-gestures (`ui/Notifications`), WebAuthn (`SecuritySettings`),\n573:   `DatePicker`/`MultiSelect`, dompurify/marked-rich components, electronAPI\n574:   (`TitleBar`/`UpdateChecker`), clipboard API (`ClipboardList`).\n575: - `ImageService.resizeImage` (canvas + `Image`).\n576: - Icons, logos, and other render-only components.\n577: - Third-party behavior — assert our props/logic, not ECharts/ProseMirror internals.\n578: - E2E/Playwright for now — a client-side SPA with a mocked API at the unit level\n579:   is already covered by store + component tests; E2E adds infrastructure for\n580:   marginal value.\n581: \n582: ### Execution order\n583: \n584: 1. [x] `Calendars` + `Auth` store tests (biggest logic; recipe proven) — TASK-1/TASK-2.\n585: 2. [x] `Notes` + library-store filtering tests — TASK-3/TASK-4 (+ `CheckInData`, TASK-5).\n586: 3. [x] §4.3 context harness — TASK-6.\n587: 4. [x] Dashboard widgets + logic-bearing leaves — TASK-7/TASK-8.\n588: 5. [x] Translation-only components — TASK-9.\n589: 6. [x] Re-run `npm run test:coverage` and inspect the remaining uncovered lines —\n590:    they cluster in the \"explicitly out of scope\" list above (plus the secondary\n591:    stores named in §0). The suite is \"complete enough\" rather than \"maximised\",\n592:    which is the goal.\n593: 7. [x] Optional follow-up: secondary stores with real non-CRUD logic — `Feeds`,\n594:    `Contacts`, `Navigation` (+ `PUBLIC_DISABLE_DEV_REQUESTS` env branch),\n595:    `QuickAdd`, `UserNotifications`, `WelcomeTour`, `Theme` (DOM-stubbed),\n596:    `PwaInstall`. All landed in `tests/unit/stores/` and brought `lib/state`\n597:    statement coverage to ~56%.\n\n(End of file - total 597 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Test coverage plan\n\nHow to build the best possible automated test coverage for the solyto frontend.\n\nStatus of this document: proposal. Nothing here is implemented yet. The phases\nat the bottom describe the order of work; every phase that requires new\ndev-dependencies needs explicit approval before `npm install` (dependencies are\npinned, `engine-strict=true`).\n\n---\n\n## 0. Implementation status\n\nMost of the plan below is now implemented. Current state (run `npm test`):\n\n- **678 tests** (53 files) across 3 Vitest projects: `unit` (node), `stores`\n  (node + store-mock setup), `components` (jsdom).\n- Coverage: `src/lib` at **~22.8% statements / ~29.2% functions / ~22.2%\n  lines** (up from 8.7% / 12.4%), against the whole of `src/lib` including\n  the 357 untested components and 37 stores. The remaining uncovered lines","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/TESTING.md","text":"# Test coverage plan\n\nHow to build the best possible automated test coverage for the solyto frontend.\n\nStatus of this document: proposal. Nothing here is implemented yet. The phases\nat the bottom describe the order of work; every phase that requires new\ndev-dependencies needs explicit approval before `npm install` (dependencies are\npinned, `engine-strict=true`).\n\n---\n\n## 0. Implementation status\n\nMost of the plan below is now implemented. Current state (run `npm test`):\n\n- **678 tests** (53 files) across 3 Vitest projects: `unit` (node), `stores`\n  (node + store-mock setup), `components` (jsdom).\n- Coverage: `src/lib` at **~22.8% statements / ~29.2% functions / ~22.2%\n  lines** (up from 8.7% / 12.4%), against the whole of `src/lib` including\n  the 357 untested components and 37 stores. The remaining uncovered lines\n  cluster in the documented out-of-scope list (§8) — heavy/skip components\n  (echarts, TipTap, DnD, WebAuthn, electronAPI, …) and the boilerplate CRUD\n  stores — which is the intended \"complete enough\" state.\n- New devDeps (pinned): `@vitest/coverage-v8`, `jsdom`, `@testing-library/svelte`,\n  `@testing-library/jest-dom`, `@testing-library/user-event`, `@testing-library/dom`.\n- `vitest.config.ts` now uses `sveltekit()` + three projects; `tests/unit/setup/storeMocks.ts`\n  registers module mocks (ApiService/Auth/LocalStorageService/`$app/state`) for the\n  `stores` project only, so service-boundary tests keep the real implementations.\n- `Todos` and `Finances` state classes received a constructor-injection refactor\n  (auth/apiService/localStorage), defaulting to current behaviour. Other stores\n  are tested without source changes via the store mocks.\n- Component tests run in jsdom with `resolve.conditions: ['browser']` (needed so\n  `svelte` resolves to the client build, not SSR) and an `Element.prototype.animate`\n  stub in `tests/setup/component.ts` for Svelte transitions.\n\n### Covered so far\n\n- **Pure logic (Phase 1):** `TodoGroupingService`, `TodoRelevanceService`,\n  `LibraryFilterService`, `WealthStatisticsService`, `TodoFilterService` gaps\n  (`filterCategoriesByHideIt`, `due: 'week'`), `CheckInHelper`,\n  `CheckInSummaryHelper`, `ColorHelper`, `FormatHelper`, `NameHelper`, full\n  `DateHelper` gap coverage, `NumberHelper.europeanFormat`, all `MusicTheory/*`,\n  `themes.ts`, `confetti.ts`.\n- **Service boundary (Phase 2):** `ApiService` (fetch seam — headers, `%s`/`%d`\n  replacement, method/body semantics, error paths), `LocalStorageService`,\n  `NavHelper`, `platform.ts`, `urls.ts`, `features.ts`.\n- **Stores (Phase 3):** `Todos`, `Finances`, `Tags`, `UserManagement`,\n  `TimeTracking`, `LoadingIndicator`, `CookieConsent`, `UiNotifications`,\n  `Calendars` (42-day grid, per-date lookups, month/week/day navigation,\n  view-state persistence), `Auth` (login/register/refresh/passkey,\n  load-from-localStorage, `isAdmin`, `shouldRefresh` threshold, public-profile\n  cache — in `tests/unit/auth/` because the stores project's storeMocks\n  replaces the Auth module), `Notes` (newest/updated/favorites, category\n  lookup/titles, collapsed persistence, `selectNote`, url-active check,\n  create guards), all 8 library stores' **filtering** (search,\n  genre/rating/type/location, wishlist/lent/unidentified flags,\n  view-pref persistence, LinkLibrary category counts), `CheckInData`\n  (month navigation with year wrap, `isCurrentMonth`, date-derived\n  `selectedDate`, scored-trackers persistence, settings merge).\n- **Auth-token workflow regression:** `tests/unit/auth/AuthTokenFlow.test.ts`\n  pins the token snapshot semantics — `new Todos()`/`new Finances()` capture\n  `auth.getToken()` into their `ApiService` at construction (and send it as a\n  Bearer header), guarding the store-construction ordering workflow described\n  in §0's Docker note's sibling docs.\n- **Components (Phase 4a):** forms (`Checkbox`, `TextInput`, `Toggle`, `Select`),\n  ui primitives (`Heading`, `Badge`, `CloseButton`, `DeleteButton`, `AddButton`,\n  `ViewSwitcher`), `todos/Counter`, and logic leaves (`AverageNumber`, `Rating`,\n  `StatisticWidget`).\n- **Context harness (§4.3):** `tests/components/helpers/context.ts` +\n  `ContextHarness.svelte` seed `setTranslation`, `setKeyManager`, `setTodos`,\n  `setAuth`, `setLoadingIndicator`, `setUiNotifications`, `setViewPoint`,\n  `setCookieConsent` before rendering — unlocks the context-coupled component\n  tests below. `tests/setup/component.ts` additionally stubs\n  `Element.prototype.animate` (completing `onfinish`), `matchMedia` and the\n  `$env/dynamic/public` virtual module.\n- **Components (Phase 4b/4c):** dashboard widgets (`DueTodosWidget`,\n  `ScoredTodosWidget`, `EventsTodayWidget`, `UpcomingEventsWidget`,\n  `NewestNotesWidget`, `NewestLinksWidget`, `BookReleasesWidget`,\n  `MovieReleasesWidget`, `MusicReleasesWidget`, `QuoteWidget`), logic-bearing\n  leaves (`forms/InputAutocomplete`, `forms/InlineAutocomplete`, `forms/Slider`,\n  `todos/NoTodos`, `check-in/DailyCheckInIcon` + `check-in/overview/CheckInIcon`,\n  `libraries/shared/GenreFlexList`, `tags/TagFlexList`,\n  `libraries/shared/CoverImage`), and translation-only components\n  (  `PasswordInput`, `PasswordStrengthIndicator`, `PasswordMatchIndicator`,\n  `ui/CookieBanner`, `NavLegalEntry`, `PopupConfirmationModal`,\n  `BottomSheetConfirmationModal`, `ImportButton` + 8 provider variants:\n  Goodreads/Hardcover/Bgg/Steam/Deezer/Discogs/Imdb/Chefkoch).\n- **Secondary stores (TASK-11):** `Feeds` (loadMore pagination/recursion,\n  filter, library flags, subscribe duplicates), `Contacts` (`contactsAZ`\n  grouping/sorting/hidden books, search, photo batching), `Navigation`\n  (usage tracking, `promoteMobileItem` least-used swap), `QuickAdd`\n  (detect/auto-confirm/error branches, `isUrl`), `UserNotifications`\n  (unread, mark-all-read, polling with fake timers), `WelcomeTour` (step\n  building, navigation), `Theme` (load/apply/persist, dark-mode listener,\n  `patchAnimate` — with document/window/Element stubs), `PwaInstall`\n  (capture/install flow, iOS detection).\n\n### Not yet covered\n\nThe refined next-steps roadmap (§8, Priority 1–3 and the execution order) is\nnow implemented: state stores with real business logic (including the\nsecondary stores `Feeds`, `Contacts`, `Navigation`, `QuickAdd`,\n`UserNotifications`, `WelcomeTour`, `Theme`, `PwaInstall`), the context\nharness, dashboard widgets, logic-bearing leaves and the translation-only\ncomponents. What remains untested is deliberately out of scope (see §8): the\nheavy/skip component list (§4d — echarts, TipTap/ProseMirror, DnD,\nsvelte-gestures, WebAuthn, electronAPI, clipboard API, canvas), render-only\ncomponents, and the remaining boilerplate CRUD store wrappers (`Clipboard`,\n`DevRequests`, `Friends`, `LibraryNavigation`, `Shortcuts`, `Statistics`,\n`Weather`). E2E (Phase 5) is deliberately out of scope for now — see §8.\n\n### Docker decision\n\nThe frontend does **not** get an API-style test image. The backend's one-shot\n`test` container exists because PHP needs `pcov` and only ever runs in Docker;\nthe frontend test suite is 100% in-process (mocked fetch), so a test container\nwould add orchestration with zero isolation — and the compose bind-mount of\n`../app/:/app` means a test container runs the host's `node_modules` anyway.\nFrontend tests run on the host via Vitest. Docker only enters at the future\nintegration/E2E layer, which needs the full stack up (api/nginx at `:8000`).\n\n---\n\n## 1. Current state\n\n- Vitest 4.1.8 with `environment: 'node'`, `env: { TZ: 'UTC' }`, `$lib` alias,\n  `include: ['tests/**/*.test.ts']`.\n- 74 passing tests in 4 files, all **pure functions**:\n    - `tests/helpers/DateHelper.test.ts`, `tests/helpers/NumberHelper.test.ts`\n    - `tests/services/TodoFilterService.test.ts`, `tests/services/TodoSortingService.test.ts`\n- No component tests, no state-store tests, no E2E tests. `@testing-library/svelte`,\n  `jsdom`/`happy-dom`, Playwright, and coverage tooling are not installed.\n\n### Two blockers that gate everything (empirically verified)\n\n1. **`.svelte.ts` files cannot be imported in the current Vitest config.**\n   Importing any `src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts` throws `ReferenceError: $state is\nnot defined`, because the Svelte compiler plugin is not active in Vitest.\n   Verified with a throwaway test against `LoadingIndicator.svelte.ts`.\n2. **`$app/*` and `$env/*` modules are unresolvable** (no SvelteKit aliases),\n   unless each test `vi.mock`s them. `$env/dynamic/public` is imported at\n   module load by `src/lib/config/platform.ts`, so it blocks everything\n   transitively (e.g. `apiRoutes.ts`).\n\nVerified working recipe: adding `@sveltejs/vite-plugin-svelte` to the Vitest\nconfig compiles runes in `.svelte.ts`, and `vi.mock`ing `$app/state`,\n`$app/environment`, `$env/dynamic/public`, `$lib/state/Auth.svelte`,\n`$lib/services/ApiService`, and `$lib/services/LocalStorageService` lets the\nstate classes be instantiated and tested in node. (Confirmed: `new Todos()`\nworks under that recipe.)\n\n### Architecture facts that shape the strategy\n\n- **Pure client-side-rendered SPA.** There are zero `load` functions, no\n  `+server.ts`, no `+page.ts`/`+layout.ts`, no `hooks.server.ts`, no\n  `*.server.*` files anywhere in `src/routes`. All data is fetched in\n  `onMount` handlers that call `.load()` on state stores.\n- **Data flow:** component → state store (`src/lib/state/*.svelte.ts`) →\n  `ApiService` (`src/lib/services/ApiService.ts`) → REST API at\n  `${getApiUrl()}/api/v1` (`http://localhost:8000` in dev). `ApiService` is a\n  single fetch choke point — one seam to stub for the entire app.\n- **Stores are Svelte-context singletons:** 37 runes classes, created in\n  `src/routes/+layout.svelte` via `setX()`, read back via `getX()`.\n    - 29 of 37 call `getAuth()` at **class-field initialisation** (so even\n      `new X()` fails without a mocked Auth module or injected auth).\n    - 28 construct `new ApiService(...)` internally; 12 construct\n      `new LocalStorageService()`; 8 construct `new LibraryFilterService()`.\n    - 5 use `page` from `$app/state` (CheckInData, Finances, LibraryNavigation,\n      Notes, Todos); 3 use `browser` from `$app/environment`.\n    - `QuickAdd` additionally reads `getTranslation()` and `getUiNotifications()`.\n- **No DI anywhere:** stores build their own services in the constructor.\n  Field initializers run _before_ the constructor body, so adding constructor\n  parameters alone is not enough — the initializer must move into the\n  constructor (see §4).\n- **Service worker** (`src/service-worker.ts`) precaches the app shell and\n  uses stale-while-revalidate, but explicitly skips `/api` GETs. It does not\n  affect API mocking; it can serve stale shell during E2E runs and should be\n  blocked/cleared there.\n- The only type modules with runtime values are `src/lib/types/check_in.ts`\n  and `src/lib/types/quick_add.ts`; all other type files are erased at compile\n  time.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Strategy: a four-layer test pyramid\n\nThe most coverage per effort, in order:\n\n```\n               ┌─────────────┐\n               │  E2E (later)│  Playwright, mocked API — a few happy paths\n               └─────────────┘\n            ┌─────────────────────┐\n            │ Component (jsdom)   │  @testing-library/svelte — pure leaves,\n            │  + integration      │  then context-harnessed feature tests\n            └─────────────────────┘\n         ┌────────────────────────────┐\n         │  Unit: state stores        │  node + module mocks (+ small DI refactor)\n         └────────────────────────────┘\n      ┌───────────────────────────────────┐\n      │  Unit: pure logic (helpers,       │  node — biggest cheap win\n      │  services, config, ApiService)    │\n      └───────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\nLayer 1 and the pure part of layer 2 require **no new dependencies** (except a\ncoverage reporter). Layers 2–4 require the infrastructure changes in §3.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Required infrastructure changes (enable first)\n\n### 3.1 Fix the Vitest config (`vitest.config.ts`)\n\nAdd the Svelte compiler plugin so `.svelte.ts` and `.svelte` files compile:\n\n```ts\nimport { sveltekit } from '@sveltejs/kit/vite';\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vitest/config';\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n\tplugins: [sveltekit()],\n\tresolve: { alias: { $lib: resolve('./src/lib') } },\n\ttest: {\n\t\tinclude: ['tests/**/*.test.ts'],\n\t\tenvironment: 'node',\n\t\tenv: { TZ: 'UTC' }\n\t}\n});\n```\n\n- `sveltekit()` is the documented SvelteKit approach: it activates the Svelte\n  plugin (fixes `$state` in `.svelte.ts`) **and** makes `$app/*`/`$env/*`\n  resolvable, so most tests won't need to mock those.\n- Alternative if `sveltekit()` proves problematic in Vitest: use\n  `svelte({ compilerOptions: { runes: true } })` and `vi.mock` each `$app/*`\n  / `$env/*` module per test (verified working).\n- `$app/environment`'s `browser` flag may report `false` under node/jsdom\n  depending on the SvelteKit version — tests that need `browser === true`\n  (e.g. `LocalStorageService`) should force it:\n  `vi.mock('$app/environment', () => ({ browser: true, dev: true }))`.\n\n### 3.2 Add a jsdom project for component tests\n\nVitest 4 supports `projects`. Add a second project so the existing node tests\nstay untouched:\n\n```ts\ntest: {\n\tprojects: [\n\t\t{ test: { include: ['tests/**/*.test.ts'], environment: 'node' } },\n\t\t{\n\t\t\tplugins: [sveltekit()],\n\t\t\ttest: {\n\t\t\t\tinclude: ['tests/components/**/*.test.ts'],\n\t\t\t\tenvironment: 'jsdom',\n\t\t\t\tsetupFiles: ['tests/setup/component.ts']\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t];\n}\n```\n\nComponent tests live under `tests/components/` and run in jsdom.\n\n### 3.3 New dev-dependencies (all require approval before install)\n\n| Package                       | Purpose                                  | Version notes         |\n| ----------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- | --------------------- |\n| `@vitest/coverage-v8`         | `--coverage` reporting to drive the plan | match vitest 4.x      |\n| `jsdom`                       | DOM for component tests                  | latest                |\n| `@testing-library/svelte`     | render Svelte 5 components               | v5+ supports Svelte 5 |\n| `@testing-library/jest-dom`   | DOM matchers (`toBeInTheDocument`, ...)  | v6                    |\n| `@testing-library/user-event` | realistic clicks/typing                  | v14                   |\n| _(later)_ `@playwright/test`  | E2E layer                                | optional, phase 5     |\n\n### 3.4 Test support code (`tests/` layout)\n\n```\ntests/\n  setup/component.ts        # jest-dom import, localStorage/global stubs, cleanup\n  helpers/\n    factories.ts            # todo(), category(), tag(), checkIn() builders\n    context.ts              # renderWithContext(component, { stores }) — see §4.3\n    fetchMock.ts            # mockFetch(routes) + ApiService fake\n    localStorageMock.ts     # in-memory localStorage\n  unit/                     # node env: helpers, services, config, stores\n  components/               # jsdom env: component tests\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Making the state layer testable (small refactor, big payoff)\n\nThe stores hold most of the app's real logic (`Todos.useFilters`,\n`Todos.groupByStatus`, `Finances.getWealthSum`, library search/filter, ...) and\nare currently untestable because services are constructed internally and `auth`\nis a context read at field-init. The minimal, mechanical refactor:\n\n```ts\n// before — field initializer runs before the constructor body\nexport class Todos {\n\tauth = getAuth();\n\tapiService: ApiService;\n\tlocalStorage = new LocalStorageService();\n\tconstructor() {\n\t\tthis.apiService = new ApiService(this.auth.getToken());\n\t}\n}\n\n// after — everything injectable, defaults preserve current behaviour\nexport class Todos {\n\tauth: Auth;\n\tapiService: ApiService;\n\tlocalStorage: LocalStorageService;\n\tconstructor(\n\t\tauth: Auth = getAuth(),\n\t\tapiService: ApiService = new ApiService(auth.getToken()),\n\t\tlocalStorage: LocalStorageService = new LocalStorageService()\n\t) {\n\t\tthis.auth = auth;\n\t\tthis.apiService = apiService;\n\t\tthis.localStorage = localStorage;\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nThis applies to:\n\n- **28 stores** constructing `ApiService`: pass it in (Auth, Todos, Notes,\n  Calendars, Finances, Feeds, all 8 libraries, Contacts, CheckInData,\n  Clipboard, DevRequests, Friends, Shortcuts, Statistics, Tags, TimeTracking,\n  UserManagement, UserNotifications, Weather, Navigation, QuickAdd).\n- **12 stores** constructing `LocalStorageService` (incl. Auth, Theme,\n  CookieConsent).\n- **8 library stores** constructing `LibraryFilterService`.\n- **QuickAdd**: inject `ts`/`notifications` as well.\n- **Stores using `page` from `$app/state`**: keep reading `page` for now and\n  `vi.mock('$app/state')` in tests; or inject a `getPathname`/`page` for the\n  cleanest seams (only 5 stores; the constructor only reads path params, not a\n  live value).\n\nScope guard: this refactor is mechanical and does not change behaviour. Do it\nonly as far as tests need it (one store at a time), not as a bulk rewrite.\n\n### 4.1 Standard unit-test recipe for a store\n\n```ts\nvi.mock('$app/state', () => ({ page: { url: new URL('http://localhost/todos') } }));\nvi.mock('$lib/state/Auth.svelte', () => ({\n  getAuth: () => ({ getToken: () => 'test-token', /* …used methods */ })\n}));\nvi.mock('$lib/services/ApiService', () => ({\n  default: class FakeApi {\n    list = vi.fn(); get = vi.fn(); create = vi.fn();\n    update = vi.fn(); delete = vi.fn(); post = vi.fn(); put = vi.fn();\n  }\n}));\n\nconst api = new (await import('$lib/services/ApiService')).default();\nconst store = new Todos(/* mocked auth */, api as any, /* fake storage */);\n\n// test pure logic: set store.todos, call useFilters(), assert store.filteredTodos\n// test CRUD: api.list.mockResolvedValue({ data: [...] }); await store.load();\n```\n\nMock only the methods a given test exercises; `ApiService` methods return\n`null` by default (safe no-ops) unless stubbed.\n\n### 4.2 Priority stores to test first (highest logic density)\n\n| Store                                                                                                                         | What to cover                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Todos.svelte.ts`                                                                                                             | `useFilters` (backlog/hide-it/category/tag/auto-generated visibility), `groupByStatus`, `checkUrlForFilter`, `quickCreate` recurrence-ignore logic, `toggleSortByScore`, `loadHideIt` |\n| `Finances.svelte.ts`                                                                                                          | `getWealthSum`, `getBudgetTotal`, `getBudgetIncomeTotal`, `getBudgetExpenseTotal`, `getActivePage`, `loadIncome` income/expense split                                                 |\n| `Auth.svelte.ts`                                                                                                              | token refresh flow, `isAdmin`, login/register request bodies, persistence keys                                                                                                        |\n| `Calendars.svelte.ts`                                                                                                         | `loadMonth` date math, `getEventsForDate`, view state (skip the 3 direct `fetch` methods or stub global fetch)                                                                        |\n| Library stores (BookLibrary, MusicLibrary, MovieLibrary, GameLibrary, PlantLibrary, QuoteLibrary, RecipeLibrary, LinkLibrary) | search/filter by genre/rating/type/location, wishlist/lent/unidentified flags, per-type `*View` prefs from localStorage                                                               |\n| `Notes.svelte.ts`                                                                                                             | `getNewestNotes`, `getCategoryTitle`, create/delete (mock `$app/navigation`/`$app/paths`)                                                                                             |\n| `CheckInData.svelte.ts`, `TimeTracking.svelte.ts`, `UserManagement.svelte.ts`, `Tags.svelte.ts`                               | pure helpers (`formatDuration`, `filterUsers`, `sort`)                                                                                                                                |\n\n### 4.3 Component test harness (context wrapper)\n\nBecause components pull stores via `getX()`, provide a render helper that\nseeds context before rendering:\n\n```ts\nimport { render } from '@testing-library/svelte';\n\nexport function renderWithContext(Component, props, stores = {}) {\n\t// wrapper component:\n\t//   setTranslation(mockTs); setKeyManager(mock); setTodos(mockTodos);\n\t//   setAuth(mockAuth); setLoadingIndicator(mock); setUiNotifications(mock);\n\t//   <Component {...props} />\n\t// store mocks = real store instances with apiService stubbed, or `vi.mock`ed modules\n}\n```\n\nBuild the wrapper once with the six most common stores (`Translation`,\n`KeyManager`, `Todos`, `Auth`, `LoadingIndicator`, `UiNotifications`) —\nunlocks ~250 context-coupled components.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Coverage roadmap (layered, in order)\n\n### Phase 1 — Complete pure-logic unit tests (node, no new deps) ✅ high ROI\n\nFinish the untested pure modules. Current gaps:\n\n**Services**\n\n- `TodoGroupingService` — `groupByStatus` (untested, pure).\n- `TodoRelevanceService` — `getScoredTodos` (pure, uses `daysSince`; use fake timers/fixed date).\n- `LibraryFilterService` — `search`, `byRating`, `byGenre`, `byGenreAndRating`, `byType`, `byLocation`, `byUnidentified`, `byWishlist`, `byLent` (pure, type-only imports).\n- `WealthStatisticsService` — `getGraphValues` (pure; `SvelteDate` + `getUrlFormat`; fix the \"current date\" with fake timers).\n- `TodoFilterService` gaps — `filterCategoriesByHideIt`, `due: 'week'` case.\n\n**Helpers**\n\n- `CheckInHelper` — `getMeanValue`, `getTotalMeanValue`.\n- `CheckInSummaryHelper` — `buildDaySummary`, `buildPeriodSummary`, `getDayLabel`.\n- `ColorHelper` — `lightenColor`.\n- `FormatHelper` — `nl2br`, `markdownToHtml` (uses `marked`, node-safe).\n- `NameHelper` — `getInitials`.\n- `MusicTheoryHelper` + all 4 `MusicTheory/*` modules (ChordGenerator, NoteOperations, ScaleGenerator, TheoryConstants) — large pure surface, snapshot the constants.\n- `DateHelper` gaps (~14 functions): `formatDateWithWeekday`, `formatFloatingDate`, `getUrlFormat`, `getDaysInMonth`, `getLast30Days`, `getNextXDays`, `isDateThisWeek`, `isDateLast7Days`, `getCurrentTimestamp`, `getCurrentYearMonthString`, `getISODateInfo`, `getCalendarMonth`, `getCalendarWeek`, `dateFromTimestamp`.\n- `NumberHelper` gap — `europeanFormat`.\n\n**Config / effects**\n\n- `themes.ts` — pure data.\n- `effects/confetti.ts` — `createConfettiOptions` merges options (type-only import, pure).\n\n### Phase 2 — Service boundary tests (node, tiny mocks)\n\n- `ApiService` — stub `globalThis.fetch` (`vi.stubGlobal`): assert `list/get/create/delete/update/post/put/postFormData/uploadFile` send the right method, URL (`%s`/`%d` replacement), headers (Bearer token present/absent, Content-Type for bodies), and return semantics on `ok`/error. This is the single most valuable test target — it is the only network seam.\n- `LocalStorageService` — `vi.mock('$app/environment', () => ({ browser: true }))` + in-memory `localStorage` stub; assert get/set/getJson/getNumber/getBool/destroy round-trips and JSON parse-failure → null.\n- `NavHelper` — `vi.mock('$app/state')`; cover `getPageSlug`, `getPageFeature`, `showNavbar`, `isDashboard`, `isAdminRoute`, `isAuthRoute`, `isSetupRoute`.\n- `platform.ts` / `urls.ts` / `features.ts` / `navigation.ts` / `apiRoutes.ts` — `vi.mock('$env/dynamic/public')` + `$app/*` + `localStorage`; assert `getApiUrl` resolution order (env → hostname map → fallback), custom-API URL persistence, `PLATFORM`/`IS_NATIVE` flags. Use `vi.resetModules()` + fresh `$env` mocks for isolation.\n\n### Phase 3 — State stores (node + module mocks, after §4 refactor)\n\nApply the §4.1 recipe. Full inventory by group (37 files):\n\n| Group            | Stores                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | Extra mocks needed                                                                                                                             |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Root             | `Auth`                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | `$env/dynamic/public`, ApiService, LocalStorageService                                                                                         |\n| No-auth (8)      | `LoadingIndicator`, `UiNotifications`, `WelcomeTour`, `PwaInstall`, `Viewpoint`, `CookieConsent`, `Theme`, `LibraryNavigation`                                                                                                                                                                                                           | `LoadingIndicator` testable as-is; `WelcomeTour`/`LibraryNavigation` need `urls`/`$app/state` mocks; `Theme` DOM methods need jsdom or adapter |\n| Auth+CRUD (21)   | `Todos`, `Notes`, `Calendars`, `Finances`, `Feeds`, `Contacts`, `BookLibrary`, `MusicLibrary`, `MovieLibrary`, `GameLibrary`, `PlantLibrary`, `QuoteLibrary`, `RecipeLibrary`, `LinkLibrary`, `Clipboard`, `DevRequests`, `Friends`, `Shortcuts`, `Statistics`, `Tags`, `TimeTracking`, `UserManagement`, `UserNotifications`, `Weather` | Auth + ApiService (+ LocalStorageService for the 12 that use it)                                                                               |\n| `page` users (5) | CheckInData, Finances, LibraryNavigation, Notes, Todos                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | `$app/state`                                                                                                                                   |\n| Special          | `QuickAdd` (3 contexts), `Navigation` (`$env/dynamic/public` + `auth.user.settings`), `Translation` (`browser` + `navigator.language`)                                                                                                                                                                                                   | per-file                                                                                                                                       |\n\n### Phase 4 — Component tests (jsdom, after §3.2/§3.3)\n\n**4a. Pure/presentational leaves (~70, low effort).** No context, no `$app`:\n\n- `forms/` (11): Checkbox, DateInput, DateTimeInput, NumberInput, TextInput, Select, Slider, Toggle, SvelteDateInput, InputAutocomplete, InlineAutocomplete.\n- `ui/buttons/` (17): AcceptButton, AddButton, CloseButton, CloudButton, DeleteButton, EditButton, FunnelButton, HamburgerButton, IconButton, ImportButton, InlineDeleteButton, InlineEditButton, InlineExpandButton, RefreshButton, SaveButton, StarButton, TextButton.\n- `ui/icons/` (12), `ui/menus/` (2: MenuIcon, RightClickMenu), `ui/` primitives (~18): Badge, Card, Divider, File, Flag, Heading, SubHeading, ModalFormRow, Tabs, ViewSwitcher, NavEntry, NavEntryIcon, MovableHoverBox, HelpTooltip, LoadingLogo, StaggeredLogo, QuickSelectOverlay, PopupContentModal, BottomSheetModal, SlidingSideBar.\n- Feature leaves: `todos/Counter`, `check-in/` (DailyCheckInIcon, CheckInIcon, AverageNumber), `libraries/shared/` (Rating, CoverImage, MissingCover, GenreFlexList, ExternalSearchLink, BookRelease), `tags/TagFlexList`, `dev-requests/Author`, `guitar/GuitarTheoryNavigation`, `admin/StatisticWidget`, `notes/AddFolderButton`/`AddNoteButton`/`editor/ToolbarDivider`, `settings/SettingsSection` + SettingsNavigation*, `dashboard/widgets/*` (the props-driven ones: DueTodosWidget, ScoredTodosWidget, EventsTodayWidget, UpcomingEventsWidget, NewestNotesWidget, NewestLinksWidget, BookReleasesWidget, MovieReleasesWidget, MusicReleasesWidget, QuoteWidget).\n\n**4b. Translation-only components (~20).** Presentational but call `getTranslation()`; become trivial once the §4.3 harness exists: the `*ImportButton`/`*Button` icons, `NoTodos`, `PasswordInput`, `PasswordStrengthIndicator`, `PasswordMatchIndicator`, `ui/CookieBanner`, `PopupConfirmationModal`, `BottomSheetConfirmationModal`, `NavLegalEntry`.\n\n**4c. KeyManager + domain integration.** With `setKeyManager()`/`setTodos()`/`setAuth()`/`setLoadingIndicator()`/`setUiNotifications()`/`setViewPoint()` in the harness:\n\n- Todos feature: `views/{CardView,ListView,OverviewView}`, `props/*` (Category, DueDate, Effort, Flags, Link, Priority, Progress, Recurrence, Status, Subtasks, Tags, Title), `actions/{TodoCreate,TodoDelete,HideIt,SortByScore}`, `TodoNavigation*`, `ListAndAdd`.\n- Calendars: `views/{day,week,month,list}/*`, `NavigationEntry`, `MobileCalendarHeader`.\n- Dashboard: `YourDay`, `QuickGlance`, plus context widgets.\n- Libraries: shared `Entries/Header/Search/ShelfView/SpineView/CreateModal/DetailModal`.\n- Feeds, time-tracking, notes, check-in, settings, finances as capacity allows.\n\n**4d. Heavy/skip (~15 components).** Do not attempt in jsdom without heavy stubbing — exclude from automated coverage or stub their leaf dependencies:\n`charts/*` (echarts), `notes/editor/*` (TipTap/ProseMirror), `todos/views/KanbanView` (svelte-dnd-action), `ui/Notifications` (svelte-gestures), `settings/SecuritySettings` (simplewebauthn), `forms/{DatePicker,MultiSelect}` (datepicker/svelte-multiselect), `settings/{TagEdit,LocalizationSettings}`, `contacts/AddressBook*` (color picker, tzdb), dompurify/marked-rich components, `desktop/TitleBar` + `settings/UpdateChecker` (electronAPI), `clipboard/ClipboardList` (clipboard API), `tour/WelcomeTour`, `quick-add/QuickAddModal`. `ImageService.resizeImage` (canvas) is likewise skipped or reduced to pure resize-math.\n\n### Phase 5 — E2E (optional, later)\n\nIf desired, Playwright against the real dev server with API responses mocked at\n`http://localhost:8000/api/v1/**` (or via a stub server). High-value flows:\nauth (email/password + WebAuthn virtual authenticator), todos CRUD, calendar\nmonth navigation, a library search. Must block/clear the service-worker cache\n(`serviceWorkers: 'block'` or `caches.delete()`) for deterministic runs.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Expected coverage & measurement\n\n- Use `@vitest/coverage-v8` with `npm run test:coverage`.\n- Treat coverage as a **signal, not a target**: after the §8 roadmap, the\n  remaining uncovered code should be the explicit out-of-scope list — third-party\n  wrappers, canvas/DOM-heavy leaves, and render-only components.\n- Keep the out-of-scope paths excluded (`exclude` in the coverage config) so\n  the number stays honest and comparable over time.\n- Re-measure after each priority and watch _where_ the uncovered lines are,\n  not the headline percentage. The number will stay modest while the 357\n  components and 37 stores exist, because most of them are intentionally not\n  tested (see §8).\n\n## 7. Risks & caveats\n\n- **SvelteKit `$app/state` `page` object** in tests is a static mock; code that\n  reacts to `page` changes won't be exercised at unit level (fine — component\n  tests cover rendering paths).\n- **Run/effect timing:** stores use `setTimeout`/`tick`/`setInterval`\n  (`quickCreate`, `recentlyCreated`, `UserNotifications`, `Calendars`,\n  `Notes`). Use `vi.useFakeTimers()` and `flushSync`/`await tick()`.\n- **`SvelteDate` ignores `vi.setSystemTime`:** `svelte/reactivity`'s `SvelteDate`\n  captures the native `Date` at module load (in both the client and server\n  builds), so the fake-timer clock never reaches `new SvelteDate()` — it always\n  returns the real current time. Tests that exercise store code reading \"now\"\n  via `SvelteDate` (`Calendars` constructor/`goToToday`, `CheckInData`\n  initialisation/`isCurrentMonth`) must therefore assert against the real\n  `new Date()` on real timers, never against a hardcoded date — a hardcoded\n  \"today\" only passes on the day it was written.\n- **jsdom gaps:** `matchMedia`, `ResizeObserver`, `IntersectionObserver`,\n  `navigator.clipboard`, canvas 2D context need small stubs in\n  `tests/setup/component.ts`.\n- **i18n invariant:** when adding/verifying UI strings in component tests,\n  keep all four locales (`en/de/es/fr`) in sync — `npm run check` enforces it.\n- **Pinned deps:** all additions must be pinned and installed only with\n  approval (AGENTS.md hard rule).\n- **Do not over-test third-party wrappers:** ECharts/TipTap/DnD behavior is the\n  library's responsibility; assert our props/logic, not their internals.\n\n## 8. Next steps — where to invest next (current roadmap)\n\nGuiding rule: **test what has logic or a contract worth pinning; nothing else.**\nThe 8.7% figure is low because the denominator is the whole of `src/lib` (357\ncomponents, 37 stores), most of which is boilerplate or third-party wrappers.\nRaise it by testing the real logic — not by chasing a number.\n\n### Priority 1 — State stores with real business logic (highest value)\n\n| Store                  | What is genuinely testable                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Calendars`            | `loadMonth` (42-day grid math), `getEventsForDate`, month/week/day navigation, view state                                                                                                          |\n| `Auth`                 | login/register/refresh/passkey flows, load-from-localStorage, token-expiry branch, `isAdmin` — the security surface; the token-capture recipe is proven in `tests/unit/auth/AuthTokenFlow.test.ts` |\n| `Notes`                | `getNewestNotes`, `getCategoryTitle`, create/delete (mock `$app/navigation`/`$app/paths`)                                                                                                          |\n| Library stores (all 8) | the **non-CRUD** parts: search/filter by genre/rating/type/location, wishlist/lent/unidentified flags, view-pref persistence                                                                       |\n| `CheckInData`          | month navigation, date-derived `selectedDate`, scoring                                                                                                                                             |\n\nDo **not** test the ~20 boilerplate CRUD wrappers (`createX`/`updateX`/`deleteX`\n= call the API + reload). Prove the pattern once per store, then move on.\n\n### Priority 2 — Presentational components _with logic_\n\nMost of the ~70 \"pure\" leaves (icons, logos, dividers) are render-only and not\nworth tests. Real value is in:\n\n- Keyboard/selection logic: `forms/InputAutocomplete`, `forms/InlineAutocomplete`,\n  `forms/Slider`.\n- State-driven leaves: `todos/NoTodos`, `check-in/DailyCheckInIcon`/`CheckInIcon`,\n  `libraries/shared/GenreFlexList`, `tags/TagFlexList`, `libraries/shared/CoverImage`.\n- Props-driven dashboard widgets (`DueTodosWidget`, `ScoredTodosWidget`,\n  `UpcomingEventsWidget`, …) — data + handlers come in as props, making them the\n  cleanest integration targets in the app.\n- Translation-only components (~20 `*ImportButton`s, `NoTodos`, password\n  indicators) — only after Priority 3's harness exists.\n\n### Priority 3 — Context harness (enabling investment)\n\nOne `renderWithContext` helper that seeds `setTranslation()`, `setKeyManager()`,\n`setTodos()`, `setAuth()`, `setLoadingIndicator()`, `setUiNotifications()`,\n`setViewPoint()` before rendering (pattern in §4.3). This unlocks the ~250\ncontext-coupled components (todos views/props/actions, calendar views, dashboard)\nand the translation-only leaves. Without it, the mock boilerplate per component\ntest is not worth the effort.\n\n### Explicitly out of scope\n\n- Heavy/skip list (§4d): echarts, TipTap/ProseMirror, DnD (`KanbanView`),\n  svelte-gestures (`ui/Notifications`), WebAuthn (`SecuritySettings`),\n  `DatePicker`/`MultiSelect`, dompurify/marked-rich components, electronAPI\n  (`TitleBar`/`UpdateChecker`), clipboard API (`ClipboardList`).\n- `ImageService.resizeImage` (canvas + `Image`).\n- Icons, logos, and other render-only components.\n- Third-party behavior — assert our props/logic, not ECharts/ProseMirror internals.\n- E2E/Playwright for now — a client-side SPA with a mocked API at the unit level\n  is already covered by store + component tests; E2E adds infrastructure for\n  marginal value.\n\n### Execution order\n\n1. [x] `Calendars` + `Auth` store tests (biggest logic; recipe proven) — TASK-1/TASK-2.\n2. [x] `Notes` + library-store filtering tests — TASK-3/TASK-4 (+ `CheckInData`, TASK-5).\n3. [x] §4.3 context harness — TASK-6.\n4. [x] Dashboard widgets + logic-bearing leaves — TASK-7/TASK-8.\n5. [x] Translation-only components — TASK-9.\n6. [x] Re-run `npm run test:coverage` and inspect the remaining uncovered lines —\n   they cluster in the \"explicitly out of scope\" list above (plus the secondary\n   stores named in §0). The suite is \"complete enough\" rather than \"maximised\",\n   which is the goal.\n7. [x] Optional follow-up: secondary stores with real non-CRUD logic — `Feeds`,\n   `Contacts`, `Navigation` (+ `PUBLIC_DISABLE_DEV_REQUESTS` env branch),\n   `QuickAdd`, `UserNotifications`, `WelcomeTour`, `Theme` (DOM-stubbed),\n   `PwaInstall`. All landed in `tests/unit/stores/` and brought `lib/state`\n   statement coverage to ~56%.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":597,"totalLines":597,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/TESTING.md","time":{"start":1791709010714,"end":1791709010722}},"id":"prt_12a2ddadb0014eiMiB2iXpsyrP","sessionID":"ses_ed5d2f61fffeMvSbVSQlxsDWfl","messageID":"msg_12a2db432001SM3EKrkR7jiJLs"}}
