{"type":"text","timestamp":1791709094895,"sessionID":"ses_ed5d2f61fffeMvSbVSQlxsDWfl","part":{"id":"prt_12a2f095a001LsyEsmJjviND0v","messageID":"msg_12a2f01a00014E2JjHuUiinYSt","sessionID":"ses_ed5d2f61fffeMvSbVSQlxsDWfl","type":"text","text":"Task list written to `/workspace/docs/jobs/still_theme-appearance-mode/tasks.md`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI analyzed the brief against the actual code. Key findings that shaped the plan:\n\n- **`Theme.svelte.ts`** currently owns all dark resolution: `apply()` registers a `matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)')` listener whenever `theme.supportsDarkMode` (only `default` today) and tears it down on theme switches; `applyDark()` toggles `html.dark`. The feature slots cleanly into this file: an `appearance` `$state`, a new `LS_APPEARANCE_KEY`, `setAppearance()`, and a branching resolution in `apply()` (system → listener, forced → no listener).\n- **`AppSettings.svelte`** renders the theme picker; the segmented control belongs right there, gated on `themeState.theme.supportsDarkMode` (reactive, since `theme` is `$state`). No reusable segmented component exists — `ViewSwitcher`'s button styling is the in-repo pattern to follow.\n- **i18n** needs new `SettingsRecords` keys in `src/lib/types/translation.ts` + all four locales; `npm run check` enforces the invariant.\n- **Tests** already exist for the Theme store (`tests/unit/stores/Theme.test.ts`) pinning listener behavior. A real nuance: the store-mock `storage.get` returns one value for any key, so the new appearance read in `load()` must be mocked by key, and the forced-mode tests must verify listener add/remove — that's why TASK-4 is flagged medium risk.\n\nTasks (details in the file): TASK-1 state/appearance resolution (medium), TASK-2 i18n (low), TASK-3 settings UI (low), TASK-4 store test updates (medium), TASK-5 verification (low). No changes needed to `themes.ts` or the theme picker (out of scope for the brief).\n\nOne caveat: the environment here has no shell tool, so I could not run `git branch --show-current` to verify the job branch — I proceeded on the manigot convention that the mounted worktree is always on the job's branch (`feature/still_theme-appearance-mode`).","time":{"start":1791709088090,"end":1791709094885}}}
