{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791709107116,"sessionID":"ses_ed5d0c9e0ffeDCQju8ITYpRS1R","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_7T14m1zoW9D8bwfDAO9h4438","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/still_theme-appearance-mode/tasks.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/still_theme-appearance-mode/tasks.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Tasks: theme-appearance-mode\n2: \n3: id: still\n4: analyst: opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash\n5: date: 2026-10-11\n6: \n7: <!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n8: \n9: ## Task breakdown\n10: \n11: TASK-1: Add the app-global appearance setting to `ThemeState` and resolve effective dark from it.\n12:      files: src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts\n13:      depends: none\n14:      risk: medium — the media-query listener lifecycle (register only in `system` mode, tear down when switching to forced light/dark or to a non-dark-capable theme, keep teardown-clean across theme switches) is the delicate part; regression risk on the current OS-follow behavior, which the existing Theme store tests (TASK-4) pin.\n15: \n16: TASK-2: Add i18n keys for the appearance section and its three options (suggested `appearance`, `appearance_system`, `appearance_light`, `appearance_dark` — one key for the section label + one per Auto/Light/Dark option) to `SettingsRecords` in the translation type and all four locales.\n17:      files: src/lib/types/translation.ts, src/lib/i18n/en.ts, src/lib/i18n/de.ts, src/lib/i18n/es.ts, src/lib/i18n/fr.ts\n18:      depends: none\n19:      risk: low — mechanical additions; `npm run check` enforces the four-locale invariant.\n20: \n21: TASK-3: Render the small Auto/Light/Dark segmented control in `AppSettings.svelte`, visible only when `themeState.theme.supportsDarkMode`, bound to the new `appearance` state via `setAppearance()`.\n22:      files: src/lib/components/settings/AppSettings.svelte\n23:      depends: TASK-1, TASK-2\n24:      risk: low — presentational addition; `themeState.theme` is `$state` so the visibility gate updates reactively when the user picks a different theme. No new reusable component needed — follow the inline button styling already used by `ViewSwitcher.svelte` (rounded, `bg-c-neutral-1` / `dark:bg-s-dark-3` active state).\n25: \n26: TASK-4: Extend `tests/unit/stores/Theme.test.ts` for the new resolution logic.\n27:      files: tests/unit/stores/Theme.test.ts\n28:      depends: TASK-1\n29:      risk: medium — the shared `storage.get` mock is keyed by string, so the new appearance read in `load()` must be distinguished from the theme read (e.g. `mockImplementation` on the key, not a single return value); existing dark-mode tests must keep passing for the default `system` mode, and the DOM stubs must model listener add/remove precisely.\n30: \n31: TASK-5: Verify with `npm run check`, `npm test`, and `npm run lint`.\n32:      files: none (verification only)\n33:      depends: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4\n34:      risk: low — standard verification gate; `npm run check` is the i18n-sync gate for TASK-2.\n35: \n36: ## Notes\n37: \n38: - Theme identity vs appearance mode: `themes.ts` is untouched — no new theme variants, `supportsDarkMode` stays as-is (only `default` is dark-capable). The picker stays a picker of designs.\n39: - TASK-1 implementation guidance (matching `docs/STATE_SERVICES.md` conventions):\n40:   - New key constant `static readonly LS_APPEARANCE_KEY: string = 'appearance'` (existing keys are the bare `'theme'` / `'animations'` strings, so no `_` prefix needed).\n41:   - New `$state<'system' | 'light' | 'dark'>` field defaulting to `'system'`; restore it in `load()` (graceful fallback for unknown/absent values), persist via `this.localStorage.set(...)` in a new `setAppearance()` method that re-resolves dark immediately.\n42:   - Refactor `apply()`: theme-link loading and the `supportsDarkMode` gate stay; inside the gate, branch on appearance — `system` → existing `matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)')` + change listener; `light` → `applyDark(false)`, `dark` → `applyDark(true)`, and in both forced modes ensure any previously registered listener is removed. Non-dark-capable themes keep `classList.remove('dark')` as today.\n43:   - `html.dark` stays the single switch; `applyDark()` is unchanged.\n44:   - Optional per `docs/STATE_SERVICES.md` §Constructor injection: moving `localStorage = new LocalStorageService()` into an injectable constructor is allowed but not required — the store tests already mock the module.\n45: - `ThemeState.load()` only runs in `onMount` (`src/routes/+layout.svelte`), so browser-only DOM access is already safe; no SSR concern.\n46: - Out of scope (per brief): no new theme picker cards, no dark palettes for other themes, no per-theme appearance.\n\n(End of file - total 46 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Tasks: theme-appearance-mode\n\nid: still\nanalyst: opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash\ndate: 2026-10-11\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1: Add the app-global appearance setting to `ThemeState` and resolve effective dark from it.\n     files: src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts\n     depends: none\n     risk: medium — the media-query listener lifecycle (register only in `system` mode, tear down when switching to forced light/dark or to a non-dark-capable theme, keep teardown-clean across theme switches) is the delicate part; regression risk on the current OS-follow behavior, which the existing Theme store tests (TASK-4) pin.\n\nTASK-2: Add i18n keys for the appearance section and its three options (suggested `appearance`, `appearance_system`, `appearance_light`, `appearance_dark` — one key for the section label + one per Auto/Light/Dark option) to `SettingsRecords` in the translation type and all four locales.\n     files: src/lib/types/translation.ts, src/lib/i18n/en.ts, src/lib/i18n/de.ts, src/lib/i18n/es.ts, src/lib/i18n/fr.ts\n     depends: none\n     risk: low — mechanical additions; `npm run check` enforces the four-locale invariant.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/still_theme-appearance-mode/tasks.md","text":"# Tasks: theme-appearance-mode\n\nid: still\nanalyst: opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash\ndate: 2026-10-11\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1: Add the app-global appearance setting to `ThemeState` and resolve effective dark from it.\n     files: src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts\n     depends: none\n     risk: medium — the media-query listener lifecycle (register only in `system` mode, tear down when switching to forced light/dark or to a non-dark-capable theme, keep teardown-clean across theme switches) is the delicate part; regression risk on the current OS-follow behavior, which the existing Theme store tests (TASK-4) pin.\n\nTASK-2: Add i18n keys for the appearance section and its three options (suggested `appearance`, `appearance_system`, `appearance_light`, `appearance_dark` — one key for the section label + one per Auto/Light/Dark option) to `SettingsRecords` in the translation type and all four locales.\n     files: src/lib/types/translation.ts, src/lib/i18n/en.ts, src/lib/i18n/de.ts, src/lib/i18n/es.ts, src/lib/i18n/fr.ts\n     depends: none\n     risk: low — mechanical additions; `npm run check` enforces the four-locale invariant.\n\nTASK-3: Render the small Auto/Light/Dark segmented control in `AppSettings.svelte`, visible only when `themeState.theme.supportsDarkMode`, bound to the new `appearance` state via `setAppearance()`.\n     files: src/lib/components/settings/AppSettings.svelte\n     depends: TASK-1, TASK-2\n     risk: low — presentational addition; `themeState.theme` is `$state` so the visibility gate updates reactively when the user picks a different theme. No new reusable component needed — follow the inline button styling already used by `ViewSwitcher.svelte` (rounded, `bg-c-neutral-1` / `dark:bg-s-dark-3` active state).\n\nTASK-4: Extend `tests/unit/stores/Theme.test.ts` for the new resolution logic.\n     files: tests/unit/stores/Theme.test.ts\n     depends: TASK-1\n     risk: medium — the shared `storage.get` mock is keyed by string, so the new appearance read in `load()` must be distinguished from the theme read (e.g. `mockImplementation` on the key, not a single return value); existing dark-mode tests must keep passing for the default `system` mode, and the DOM stubs must model listener add/remove precisely.\n\nTASK-5: Verify with `npm run check`, `npm test`, and `npm run lint`.\n     files: none (verification only)\n     depends: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4\n     risk: low — standard verification gate; `npm run check` is the i18n-sync gate for TASK-2.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Theme identity vs appearance mode: `themes.ts` is untouched — no new theme variants, `supportsDarkMode` stays as-is (only `default` is dark-capable). The picker stays a picker of designs.\n- TASK-1 implementation guidance (matching `docs/STATE_SERVICES.md` conventions):\n  - New key constant `static readonly LS_APPEARANCE_KEY: string = 'appearance'` (existing keys are the bare `'theme'` / `'animations'` strings, so no `_` prefix needed).\n  - New `$state<'system' | 'light' | 'dark'>` field defaulting to `'system'`; restore it in `load()` (graceful fallback for unknown/absent values), persist via `this.localStorage.set(...)` in a new `setAppearance()` method that re-resolves dark immediately.\n  - Refactor `apply()`: theme-link loading and the `supportsDarkMode` gate stay; inside the gate, branch on appearance — `system` → existing `matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)')` + change listener; `light` → `applyDark(false)`, `dark` → `applyDark(true)`, and in both forced modes ensure any previously registered listener is removed. Non-dark-capable themes keep `classList.remove('dark')` as today.\n  - `html.dark` stays the single switch; `applyDark()` is unchanged.\n  - Optional per `docs/STATE_SERVICES.md` §Constructor injection: moving `localStorage = new LocalStorageService()` into an injectable constructor is allowed but not required — the store tests already mock the module.\n- `ThemeState.load()` only runs in `onMount` (`src/routes/+layout.svelte`), so browser-only DOM access is already safe; no SSR concern.\n- Out of scope (per brief): no new theme picker cards, no dark palettes for other themes, no per-theme appearance.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":46,"totalLines":46,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/still_theme-appearance-mode/tasks.md","time":{"start":1791709106970,"end":1791709107110}},"id":"prt_12a2f52ea001VKwuRGJUrhRcqV","sessionID":"ses_ed5d0c9e0ffeDCQju8ITYpRS1R","messageID":"msg_12a2f4cfb001n99ye3GrDFre0a"}}
