{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791709410934,"sessionID":"ses_ed5cc28c2fferyTpyy2Zhxl0sU","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_qoBnxj47Y5cumykcy2t79959","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/still_theme-appearance-mode/tasks.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/still_theme-appearance-mode/tasks.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Tasks: theme-appearance-mode\n2: \n3: id: still\n4: analyst: opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash\n5: date: 2026-10-11\n6: \n7: <!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n8: \n9: ## Task breakdown\n10: \n11: TASK-1: Add the app-global appearance setting to `ThemeState` and resolve effective dark from it.\n12:      files: src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts\n13:      depends: none\n14:      risk: medium — the media-query listener lifecycle (register only in `system` mode, tear down when switching to forced light/dark or to a non-dark-capable theme, keep teardown-clean across theme switches) is the delicate part; regression risk on the current OS-follow behavior, which the existing Theme store tests (TASK-4) pin.\n15: \n16: TASK-2: Add i18n keys for the appearance section and its three options (suggested `appearance`, `appearance_system`, `appearance_light`, `appearance_dark` — one key for the section label + one per Auto/Light/Dark option) to `SettingsRecords` in the translation type and all four locales.\n17:      files: src/lib/types/translation.ts, src/lib/i18n/en.ts, src/lib/i18n/de.ts, src/lib/i18n/es.ts, src/lib/i18n/fr.ts\n18:      depends: none\n19:      risk: low — mechanical additions; `npm run check` enforces the four-locale invariant.\n20: \n21: TASK-3: Render the small Auto/Light/Dark segmented control in `AppSettings.svelte`, visible only when `themeState.theme.supportsDarkMode`, bound to the new `appearance` state via `setAppearance()`.\n22:      files: src/lib/components/settings/AppSettings.svelte\n23:      depends: TASK-1, TASK-2\n24:      risk: low — presentational addition; `themeState.theme` is `$state` so the visibility gate updates reactively when the user picks a different theme. No new reusable component needed — follow the inline button styling already used by `ViewSwitcher.svelte` (rounded, `bg-c-neutral-1` / `dark:bg-s-dark-3` active state).\n25: \n26: TASK-4: Extend `tests/unit/stores/Theme.test.ts` for the new resolution logic.\n27:      files: tests/unit/stores/Theme.test.ts\n28:      depends: TASK-1\n29:      risk: medium — the shared `storage.get` mock is keyed by string, so the new appearance read in `load()` must be distinguished from the theme read (e.g. `mockImplementation` on the key, not a single return value); existing dark-mode tests must keep passing for the default `system` mode, and the DOM stubs must model listener add/remove precisely.\n30: \n31: TASK-5: Verify with `npm run check`, `npm test`, and `npm run lint`.\n32:      files: none (verification only)\n33:      depends: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4\n34:      risk: low — standard verification gate; `npm run check` is the i18n-sync gate for TASK-2.\n35: \n36: ## Notes\n37: \n38: - Theme identity vs appearance mode: `themes.ts` is untouched — no new theme variants, `supportsDarkMode` stays as-is (only `default` is dark-capable). The picker stays a picker of designs.\n39: - TASK-1 implementation guidance (matching `docs/STATE_SERVICES.md` conventions):\n40:   - New key constant `static readonly LS_APPEARANCE_KEY: string = 'appearance'` (existing keys are the bare `'theme'` / `'animations'` strings, so no `_` prefix needed).\n41:   - New `$state<'system' | 'light' | 'dark'>` field defaulting to `'system'`; restore it in `load()` (graceful fallback for unknown/absent values), persist via `this.localStorage.set(...)` in a new `setAppearance()` method that re-resolves dark immediately.\n42:   - Refactor `apply()`: theme-link loading and the `supportsDarkMode` gate stay; inside the gate, branch on appearance — `system` → existing `matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)')` + change listener; `light` → `applyDark(false)`, `dark` → `applyDark(true)`, and in both forced modes ensure any previously registered listener is removed. Non-dark-capable themes keep `classList.remove('dark')` as today.\n43:   - `html.dark` stays the single switch; `applyDark()` is unchanged.\n44:   - Optional per `docs/STATE_SERVICES.md` §Constructor injection: moving `localStorage = new LocalStorageService()` into an injectable constructor is allowed but not required — the store tests already mock the module.\n45: - `ThemeState.load()` only runs in `onMount` (`src/routes/+layout.svelte`), so browser-only DOM access is already safe; no SSR concern.\n46: - Out of scope (per brief): no new theme picker cards, no dark palettes for other themes, no per-theme appearance.\n\n(End of file - total 46 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Tasks: theme-appearance-mode\n\nid: still\nanalyst: opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash\ndate: 2026-10-11\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1: Add the app-global appearance setting to `ThemeState` and resolve effective dark from it.\n     files: src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts\n     depends: none\n     risk: medium — the media-query listener lifecycle (register only in `system` mode, tear down when switching to forced light/dark or to a non-dark-capable theme, keep teardown-clean across theme switches) is the delicate part; regression risk on the current OS-follow behavior, which the existing Theme store tests (TASK-4) pin.\n\nTASK-2: Add i18n keys for the appearance section and its three options (suggested `appearance`, `appearance_system`, `appearance_light`, `appearance_dark` — one key for the section label + one per Auto/Light/Dark option) to `SettingsRecords` in the translation type and all four locales.\n     files: src/lib/types/translation.ts, src/lib/i18n/en.ts, src/lib/i18n/de.ts, src/lib/i18n/es.ts, src/lib/i18n/fr.ts\n     depends: none\n     risk: low — mechanical additions; `npm run check` enforces the four-locale invariant.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/still_theme-appearance-mode/tasks.md","text":"# Tasks: theme-appearance-mode\n\nid: still\nanalyst: opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash\ndate: 2026-10-11\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1: Add the app-global appearance setting to `ThemeState` and resolve effective dark from it.\n     files: src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts\n     depends: none\n     risk: medium — the media-query listener lifecycle (register only in `system` mode, tear down when switching to forced light/dark or to a non-dark-capable theme, keep teardown-clean across theme switches) is the delicate part; regression risk on the current OS-follow behavior, which the existing Theme store tests (TASK-4) pin.\n\nTASK-2: Add i18n keys for the appearance section and its three options (suggested `appearance`, `appearance_system`, `appearance_light`, `appearance_dark` — one key for the section label + one per Auto/Light/Dark option) to `SettingsRecords` in the translation type and all four locales.\n     files: src/lib/types/translation.ts, src/lib/i18n/en.ts, src/lib/i18n/de.ts, src/lib/i18n/es.ts, src/lib/i18n/fr.ts\n     depends: none\n     risk: low — mechanical additions; `npm run check` enforces the four-locale invariant.\n\nTASK-3: Render the small Auto/Light/Dark segmented control in `AppSettings.svelte`, visible only when `themeState.theme.supportsDarkMode`, bound to the new `appearance` state via `setAppearance()`.\n     files: src/lib/components/settings/AppSettings.svelte\n     depends: TASK-1, TASK-2\n     risk: low — presentational addition; `themeState.theme` is `$state` so the visibility gate updates reactively when the user picks a different theme. No new reusable component needed — follow the inline button styling already used by `ViewSwitcher.svelte` (rounded, `bg-c-neutral-1` / `dark:bg-s-dark-3` active state).\n\nTASK-4: Extend `tests/unit/stores/Theme.test.ts` for the new resolution logic.\n     files: tests/unit/stores/Theme.test.ts\n     depends: TASK-1\n     risk: medium — the shared `storage.get` mock is keyed by string, so the new appearance read in `load()` must be distinguished from the theme read (e.g. `mockImplementation` on the key, not a single return value); existing dark-mode tests must keep passing for the default `system` mode, and the DOM stubs must model listener add/remove precisely.\n\nTASK-5: Verify with `npm run check`, `npm test`, and `npm run lint`.\n     files: none (verification only)\n     depends: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4\n     risk: low — standard verification gate; `npm run check` is the i18n-sync gate for TASK-2.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Theme identity vs appearance mode: `themes.ts` is untouched — no new theme variants, `supportsDarkMode` stays as-is (only `default` is dark-capable). The picker stays a picker of designs.\n- TASK-1 implementation guidance (matching `docs/STATE_SERVICES.md` conventions):\n  - New key constant `static readonly LS_APPEARANCE_KEY: string = 'appearance'` (existing keys are the bare `'theme'` / `'animations'` strings, so no `_` prefix needed).\n  - New `$state<'system' | 'light' | 'dark'>` field defaulting to `'system'`; restore it in `load()` (graceful fallback for unknown/absent values), persist via `this.localStorage.set(...)` in a new `setAppearance()` method that re-resolves dark immediately.\n  - Refactor `apply()`: theme-link loading and the `supportsDarkMode` gate stay; inside the gate, branch on appearance — `system` → existing `matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)')` + change listener; `light` → `applyDark(false)`, `dark` → `applyDark(true)`, and in both forced modes ensure any previously registered listener is removed. Non-dark-capable themes keep `classList.remove('dark')` as today.\n  - `html.dark` stays the single switch; `applyDark()` is unchanged.\n  - Optional per `docs/STATE_SERVICES.md` §Constructor injection: moving `localStorage = new LocalStorageService()` into an injectable constructor is allowed but not required — the store tests already mock the module.\n- `ThemeState.load()` only runs in `onMount` (`src/routes/+layout.svelte`), so browser-only DOM access is already safe; no SSR concern.\n- Out of scope (per brief): no new theme picker cards, no dark palettes for other themes, no per-theme appearance.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":46,"totalLines":46,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/still_theme-appearance-mode/tasks.md","time":{"start":1791709410799,"end":1791709410910}},"id":"prt_12a33f5d20013sGGst13E0WbFX","sessionID":"ses_ed5cc28c2fferyTpyy2Zhxl0sU","messageID":"msg_12a33eff2001fkvSA1dqFXXBWy"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791709411031,"sessionID":"ses_ed5cc28c2fferyTpyy2Zhxl0sU","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_SiHVcwc1IAfmT4lCLPkW4668","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/still_theme-appearance-mode/implementation.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/still_theme-appearance-mode/implementation.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Implementation: theme-appearance-mode\n2: \n3: id: still\n4: developer: opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash\n5: date: 2026-10-11\n6: \n7: ## Summary\n8: \n9: Added an app-global *appearance mode* (system / light / dark) that is separate\n10: from theme identity. The `Default` theme (the only one with\n11: `supportsDarkMode`) can now be forced into light or dark regardless of the OS\n12: `prefers-color-scheme`, via a small Auto/Light/Dark control in the settings\n13: page. `html.dark` remains the single switch; the OS media-query listener is\n14: still registered only in `system` mode.\n15: \n16: ## Changes\n17: \n18: TASK-1: `src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts`\n19: - Added `LS_APPEARANCE_KEY = 'appearance'` and an `appearance =\n20:   $state<'system' | 'light' | 'dark'>('system')` field.\n21: - `load()` restores the saved appearance first (unknown/absent values fall back\n22:   to `system`), then applies the theme so resolution uses the restored mode.\n23: - Added `setAppearance(mode)` — persists to LocalStorage and re-resolves dark\n24:   immediately; only touches the DOM for dark-capable themes.\n25: - Refactored `apply()`: extracted the listener teardown into\n26:   `private teardownDarkListener()` and the resolution into\n27:   `private applyAppearance()`. Inside the `supportsDarkMode` gate, `system`\n28:   registers the `matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)')` change listener as\n29:   before; `light`/`dark` force `applyDark(false/true)` with no listener.\n30:   Non-dark-capable themes still `classList.remove('dark')` exactly as before.\n31: - `applyDark()` unchanged.\n32: \n33: TASK-2: `src/lib/types/translation.ts`, `src/lib/i18n/{en,de,es,fr}.ts`\n34: - Added `appearance`, `appearance_system`, `appearance_light`,\n35:   `appearance_dark` to `SettingsRecords` and all four locale tables (section\n36:   label plus one per Auto/Light/Dark option).\n37: \n38: TASK-3: `src/lib/components/settings/AppSettings.svelte`\n39: - Added an Appearance `SettingsSection` after the theme picker, gated by\n40:   `{#if themeState.theme.supportsDarkMode}` so it is reactive to theme\n41:   switches. It renders three inline buttons (Auto / Light / Dark), following\n42:   the `ViewSwitcher.svelte` styling (`bg-c-neutral-1` /\n43:   `dark:bg-s-dark-3` active state), and calls\n44:   `themeState.setAppearance(option.value)`. Option labels come from a\n45:   `$derived` array so translations stay reactive.\n46: \n47: TASK-4: `tests/unit/stores/Theme.test.ts`\n48: - Added an `appearance` describe block: a saved forced appearance loads without\n49:   registering the OS listener; unknown values fall back to `system` (listener\n50:   registered); `setAppearance('dark')` persists and removes the existing OS\n51:   listener; forced light drops the `dark` class and adds no listener; switching\n52:   back to `system` re-registers the listener.\n53: - Existing dark-mode/system tests kept passing unchanged.\n54: \n55: TASK-5: verification\n56: - `npm run check`: 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n57: - `npm test`: 765 passed, 1 failed — see Known issues.\n58: - `npm run lint`: repo-wide prettier drift, pre-existing; ESLint passes on all\n59:   changed files (`npx eslint` exit 0).\n60: \n61: ## Known issues / follow-ups\n62: \n63: - `tests/components/logic-leaves.test.ts` > `StatisticWidget > applies the\n64:   requested color classes` fails on this branch **before** this job's changes\n65:   (the test expects `bg-blue-50`/`text-blue-600` while the component has used\n66:   theme tokens `bg-c-btn/10`/`text-c-btn` since the base commit `cc5d8ea`).\n67:   Unrelated to this job; left untouched.\n68: - `npm run lint` (`prettier --check .`) reports 484 already-unformatted files\n69:   at the base commit as well, including every file this job touches\n70:   (`translation.ts`, the four i18n files, `AppSettings.svelte`). The added lines\n71:   follow the surrounding style and ESLint is clean; the pre-existing repo-wide\n72:   formatting drift was intentionally not reformatted (out of scope).\n73: - Rendered verification via `shot` was not possible: `/settings` is\n74:   auth-gated and this environment has no API backend (no server on\n75:   `:8000`), so the app redirects to `/auth/login` before the appearance\n76:   control renders. Verification therefore relies on `svelte-check` plus the\n77:   unit tests, which pin the resolution/listener behaviour the control drives.\n\n(End of file - total 77 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Implementation: theme-appearance-mode\n\nid: still\ndeveloper: opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash\ndate: 2026-10-11\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded an app-global *appearance mode* (system / light / dark) that is separate\nfrom theme identity. The `Default` theme (the only one with\n`supportsDarkMode`) can now be forced into light or dark regardless of the OS\n`prefers-color-scheme`, via a small Auto/Light/Dark control in the settings\npage. `html.dark` remains the single switch; the OS media-query listener is\nstill registered only in `system` mode.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: `src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts`\n- Added `LS_APPEARANCE_KEY = 'appearance'` and an `appearance =\n  $state<'system' | 'light' | 'dark'>('system')` field.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/still_theme-appearance-mode/implementation.md","text":"# Implementation: theme-appearance-mode\n\nid: still\ndeveloper: opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash\ndate: 2026-10-11\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded an app-global *appearance mode* (system / light / dark) that is separate\nfrom theme identity. The `Default` theme (the only one with\n`supportsDarkMode`) can now be forced into light or dark regardless of the OS\n`prefers-color-scheme`, via a small Auto/Light/Dark control in the settings\npage. `html.dark` remains the single switch; the OS media-query listener is\nstill registered only in `system` mode.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: `src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts`\n- Added `LS_APPEARANCE_KEY = 'appearance'` and an `appearance =\n  $state<'system' | 'light' | 'dark'>('system')` field.\n- `load()` restores the saved appearance first (unknown/absent values fall back\n  to `system`), then applies the theme so resolution uses the restored mode.\n- Added `setAppearance(mode)` — persists to LocalStorage and re-resolves dark\n  immediately; only touches the DOM for dark-capable themes.\n- Refactored `apply()`: extracted the listener teardown into\n  `private teardownDarkListener()` and the resolution into\n  `private applyAppearance()`. Inside the `supportsDarkMode` gate, `system`\n  registers the `matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)')` change listener as\n  before; `light`/`dark` force `applyDark(false/true)` with no listener.\n  Non-dark-capable themes still `classList.remove('dark')` exactly as before.\n- `applyDark()` unchanged.\n\nTASK-2: `src/lib/types/translation.ts`, `src/lib/i18n/{en,de,es,fr}.ts`\n- Added `appearance`, `appearance_system`, `appearance_light`,\n  `appearance_dark` to `SettingsRecords` and all four locale tables (section\n  label plus one per Auto/Light/Dark option).\n\nTASK-3: `src/lib/components/settings/AppSettings.svelte`\n- Added an Appearance `SettingsSection` after the theme picker, gated by\n  `{#if themeState.theme.supportsDarkMode}` so it is reactive to theme\n  switches. It renders three inline buttons (Auto / Light / Dark), following\n  the `ViewSwitcher.svelte` styling (`bg-c-neutral-1` /\n  `dark:bg-s-dark-3` active state), and calls\n  `themeState.setAppearance(option.value)`. Option labels come from a\n  `$derived` array so translations stay reactive.\n\nTASK-4: `tests/unit/stores/Theme.test.ts`\n- Added an `appearance` describe block: a saved forced appearance loads without\n  registering the OS listener; unknown values fall back to `system` (listener\n  registered); `setAppearance('dark')` persists and removes the existing OS\n  listener; forced light drops the `dark` class and adds no listener; switching\n  back to `system` re-registers the listener.\n- Existing dark-mode/system tests kept passing unchanged.\n\nTASK-5: verification\n- `npm run check`: 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n- `npm test`: 765 passed, 1 failed — see Known issues.\n- `npm run lint`: repo-wide prettier drift, pre-existing; ESLint passes on all\n  changed files (`npx eslint` exit 0).\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- `tests/components/logic-leaves.test.ts` > `StatisticWidget > applies the\n  requested color classes` fails on this branch **before** this job's changes\n  (the test expects `bg-blue-50`/`text-blue-600` while the component has used\n  theme tokens `bg-c-btn/10`/`text-c-btn` since the base commit `cc5d8ea`).\n  Unrelated to this job; left untouched.\n- `npm run lint` (`prettier --check .`) reports 484 already-unformatted files\n  at the base commit as well, including every file this job touches\n  (`translation.ts`, the four i18n files, `AppSettings.svelte`). The added lines\n  follow the surrounding style and ESLint is clean; the pre-existing repo-wide\n  formatting drift was intentionally not reformatted (out of scope).\n- Rendered verification via `shot` was not possible: `/settings` is\n  auth-gated and this environment has no API backend (no server on\n  `:8000`), so the app redirects to `/auth/login` before the appearance\n  control renders. Verification therefore relies on `svelte-check` plus the\n  unit tests, which pin the resolution/listener behaviour the control drives.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":77,"totalLines":77,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/still_theme-appearance-mode/implementation.md","time":{"start":1791709410884,"end":1791709411026}},"id":"prt_12a33f5f3001smx0aIM7d3kNgj","sessionID":"ses_ed5cc28c2fferyTpyy2Zhxl0sU","messageID":"msg_12a33eff2001fkvSA1dqFXXBWy"}}
