string) =>\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tkey === ThemeState.LS_APPEARANCE_KEY ? 'sepia' : 'default'\\n\\t\\t\\t);\\n\\t\\t\\tstorage.getBool.mockReturnValue(true);\\n\\n\\t\\t\\tconst s = new ThemeState();\\n\\t\\t\\ts.load();\\n\\n\\t\\t\\texpect(s.appearance).toBe('system');\\n\\t\\t\\texpect(dom.mediaQuery.addEventListener).toHaveBeenCalledWith(\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t'change',\\n\\t\\t\\t\\texpect.any(Function)\\n\\t\\t\\t);\\n\\t\\t});\\n\\n\\t\\tit('setAppearance persists forced dark and removes the OS listener', () => {\\n\\t\\t\\tconst dom = setupDom();\\n\\t\\t\\tconst s = new ThemeState();\\n\\t\\t\\ts.apply(defaultTheme);\\n\\n\\t\\t\\ts.setAppearance('dark');\\n\\n\\t\\t\\texpect(storage.set).toHaveBeenCalledWith(ThemeState.LS_APP...\n  Line 271: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1791709385258,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ed5d0c9e0ffeDCQju8ITYpRS1R\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"write\",\"callID\":\"call_00_4YuS6WdN95aLAlQTgOCq5731\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/workspace/docs/jobs/still_theme-appearance-mode/implementation.md\",\"content\":\"# Implementation: theme-appearance-mode\\n\\nid: still\\ndeveloper: opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash\\ndate: 2026-10-11\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nAdded an app-global *appearance mode* (system / light / dark) that is separate\\nfrom theme identity. The `Default` theme (the only one with\\n`supportsDarkMode`) can now be forced into light or dark regardless of the OS\\n`prefers-color-scheme`, via a small Auto/Light/Dark control in the settings\\npage. `html.dark` remains the single switch; the OS media-query listener is\\nstill registered only in `system` mode.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\nTASK-1: `src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts`\\n- Added `LS_APPEARANCE_KEY = 'appearance'` and an `appearance =\\n  $state<'system' | 'light' | 'dark'>('system')` field.\\n- `load()` restores the saved appearance first (unknown/absent values fall back\\n  to `system`), then applies the theme so resolution uses the restored mode.\\n- Added `setAppearance(mode)` — persists to LocalStorage and re-resolves dark\\n  immediately; only touches the DOM for dark-capable themes.\\n- Refactored `apply()`: extracted the listener teardown into\\n  `private teardownDarkListener()` and the resolution into\\n  `private applyAppearance()`. Inside the `supportsDarkMode` gate, `system`\\n  registers the `matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)')` change listener as\\n  before; `light`/`dark` force `applyDark(false/true)` with no listener.\\n  Non-dark-capable themes still `classList.remove('dark')` exactly as before.\\n- `applyDark()` unchanged.\\n\\nTASK-2: `src/lib/types/translation.ts`, `src/lib/i18n/{en,de,es,fr}.ts`\\n- Added `appearance`, `appearance_system`, `appearance_light`,\\n  `appearance_dark` to `SettingsRecords` and all four locale tables (sectio...\n  Line 283: {\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791709399398,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ed5d0c9e0ffeDCQju8ITYpRS1R\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_12a33c0bb00122b1zSMBHr103k\",\"messageID\":\"msg_12a33b09a001vcYhgsWiD1HHBb\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_ed5d0c9e0ffeDCQju8ITYpRS1R\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"All tasks are complete and committed; the worktree is clean.\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nImplemented the app-global **appearance mode** for the Default theme, separating \\\"theme identity\\\" from \\\"system / forced-light / forced-dark\\\".\\n\\n**TASK-1** — `src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts`: added `LS_APPEARANCE_KEY` + `appearance = $state<'system'|'light'|'dark'>('system')`; `load()` restores it before applying the theme (unknown → `system`); new `setAppearance()` persists and re-resolves dark; refactored `apply()` so the OS media-query listener is registered **only** in `system` mode, with `light`/`dark` forcing `applyDark()` and tearing down any prior listener. `html.dark` stays the single switch.\\n\\n**TASK-2** — added `appearance` / `appearance_system` / `appearance_light` / `appearance_dark` to `SettingsRecords` and all four locales (en/de/es/fr).\\n\\n**TASK-3** — `AppSettings.svelte`: an Auto/Light/Dark segmented control shown only when `themeState.theme.supportsDarkMode`, styled after `ViewSwitcher.svelte`, labels via a reactive `$derived` array, calling `themeState.setAppearance()`.\\n\\n**TASK-4** — extended `tests/unit/stores/Theme.test.ts` (16 passing) covering saved forced mode, unknown-value fallback, listener removal/re-registration, and forced dark/light.\\n\\n**TASK-5** — `npm run check`: 0 errors/0 warnings. `npm test`: 765 passed, 1 failed. `npm run lint`: ESLint clean on changed files.\\n\\n## Verification caveats (documented in `implementation.md`)\\n- **Pre-existing failure**: `StatisticWidget > applies the requested color classes` fails at the base commit `cc5d8ea` (stale test expecting `bg-blue-50` vs. the component's theme-token classes) — unrelated, untouched.\\n- **Pre-existing prettier drift**: `npm run lint` flags 484 already-u...\n  Line 292: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1791709410934,\"sessionID\":\"ses_ed5cc28c2fferyTpyy2Zhxl0sU\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_00_qoBnxj47Y5cumykcy2t79959\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/workspace/docs/jobs/still_theme-appearance-mode/tasks.md\"},\"output\":\"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/still_theme-appearance-mode/tasks.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: # Tasks: theme-appearance-mode\\n2: \\n3: id: still\\n4: analyst: opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash\\n5: date: 2026-10-11\\n6: \\n7: <!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\\n8: \\n9: ## Task breakdown\\n10: \\n11: TASK-1: Add the app-global appearance setting to `ThemeState` and resolve effective dark from it.\\n12:      files: src/lib/state/Theme.svelte.ts\\n13:      depends: none\\n14:      risk: medium — the media-query listener lifecycle (register only in `system` mode, tear down when switching to forced light/dark or to a non-dark-capable theme, keep teardown-clean across theme switches) is the delicate part; regression risk on the current