{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791709463182,"sessionID":"ses_ed5cc28c2fferyTpyy2Zhxl0sU","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_bA9fiQB1ARmwbBioJqZv8406","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/COMPONENTS.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/COMPONENTS.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Components\n2: \n3: Policy for the UI layer: every `.svelte` component under\n4: `src/lib/components/**` and `src/routes/**`. Read\n5: [`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) first; this document applies the\n6: general rules to markup and components.\n7: \n8: ## Components are lean\n9: \n10: A component's job is to render state and forward user intent. All logic lives\n11: below it — in the state store or a pure service.\n12: \n13: - Read the stores a component needs **once at the top of `<script lang=\"ts\">`**,\n14:   never inside the markup or per-method:\n15: \n16:   ```ts\n17:   const todos = getTodos();\n18:   const loadingIndicator = getLoadingIndicator();\n19:   const keyManager = getKeyManager();\n20:   const ts = getTranslation();\n21:   ```\n22: \n23: - A component that grows a long list of `if`s and helper functions around data\n24:   has probably swallowed store logic: move it into a method on the store or a\n25:   service, then call it here. Components delegate; see\n26:   [`docs/STATE_SERVICES.md`](STATE_SERVICES.md).\n27: - Keep the `<script>` readable: store reads, `$props`, a few `$state` fields,\n28:   event handlers, `onDestroy`. If it stops being scannable, split components.\n29: \n30: ## Type props with `$props<{...}>()`\n31: \n32: Props are typed via the runes API. There is no `export let` anywhere in this\n33: codebase; do not introduce it.\n34: \n35: ```ts\n36: let { todo } = $props<{ todo: Todo }>();\n37: ```\n38: \n39: ```ts\n40: let {\n41: \tinput = $bindable(),\n42: \tvalue = $bindable(),\n43: \tplaceholder,\n44: \tonblur,\n45: \tmultiLine = false,\n46: \theight = null,\n47: \ttabindex = null\n48: } = $props<{\n49: \tinput?: HTMLInputElement | HTMLTextAreaElement | null;\n50: \tvalue: string;\n51: \tplaceholder?: string;\n52: \tonblur?: () => void;\n53: \toninput?: () => void;\n54: \tmultiLine?: boolean;\n55: \theight?: number | null;\n56: \ttabindex?: number | null;\n57: }>();\n58: ```\n59: \n60: - Use `$bindable()` only for props that the parent binds (`bind:value`); plain\n61:   props otherwise.\n62: - Event callbacks are props typed as `() => void` / `(e: Event) => void` — pass\n63:   them through with the `{onblur}` shorthand.\n64: - `let { children } = $props();` accepts the default slot fragment.\n65: \n66: ## Svelte 5 syntax only\n67: \n68: No Svelte 4 idioms. The repo has zero `on:click`, zero `createEventDispatcher`\n69: and zero `export let` — keep it that way.\n70: \n71: - Event attributes, not directives: `onclick`, `onkeydown`, `onblur`,\n72:   `onmouseover` — not `on:click`.\n73: - `{@render children?.()}` for the default slot, `{@render name()}` /\n74:   `{#snippet name()}` for named snippets.\n75: - Lifecycle: `onMount`, `onDestroy`, `$effect` imported from `svelte`.\n76: - No `createEventDispatcher`: either call a store method directly or accept an\n77:   event callback as a prop.\n78: \n79: ## Keep markup declarative — extract conditions\n80: \n81: Markup should read top-to-bottom: `{#if}` blocks for branching, `{#each}` for\n82: lists, `{value}` for output. Non-trivial conditions belong in a function or a\n83: named boolean at the top of the script, not nested inline.\n84: \n85: **Avoid** long or nested ternaries inside class attributes or other markup\n86: expressions. Example of what not to write (found in\n87: `src/lib/components/todos/props/Title.svelte`):\n88: \n89: ```svelte\n90: class=\"{todos.view === 'list'\n91: \t? 'w-9/10'\n92: \t: 'w-3/4'} rounded-lg border-1 border-c-neutral-2 text-sm …\"\n93: ```\n94: \n95: When a class or expression depends on more than a trivially-invertible fact,\n96: compute it in the script and reference the name:\n97: \n98: ```ts\n99: let inputWidth = $state('w-3/4');\n100: // derived from todos.view in a method, or:\n101: function inputClass(): string {\n102: \treturn todos.view === 'list' ? 'w-9/10' : 'w-3/4';\n103: }\n104: ```\n105: \n106: Same rule for `{#if}`: a `{#if}` whose condition spans several `&&`/`||` or\n107: requires a nest of conditions should become a named boolean or an extracted\n108: render-block function. Prefer the guard-clause style from\n109: [`BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md#early-returns--no-nested-short-ifs)\n110: where possible.\n111: \n112: ## Prefer the shared primitives\n113: \n114: Check `src/lib/components/ui/` (buttons, modals, badges, cards, navbars) and\n115: `src/lib/components/forms/` (`TextInput`, `Checkbox`, `Toggle`, `Select`,\n116: `Slider`, `DateInput`, …) before hand-rolling a control.\n117: \n118: - Reuse the existing primitives for inputs, modals, buttons and confirmation\n119:   dialogs. A hand-rolled text input with different classes than `TextInput` is\n120:   a smell.\n121: - Modal/confirm flows use the shared `Modal` primitives —\n122:   `ui/ConfirmationModal`, `ui/ContentModal`, `BottomSheetModal` for mobile.\n123: - When a primitive genuinely misses a feature, extend the shared one rather\n124:   than forking it per-feature.\n125: \n126: ## The desktop/mobile split\n127: \n128: Several features keep separate view variants driven by `Viewpoint`:\n129: \n130: - `todos/views/{ListView,CardView,OverviewView,KanbanView}` and\n131:   `todos/TodoNavigationMobile`, `todos/views/ViewSwitcher`.\n132: - `calendars/views/{day,week,month,list}`, plus `views/{day,week,month}/Mobile*View`.\n133: - Components that switch on screen class read the store once:\n134:   `const viewPoint = getViewPoint();` then branch on `viewPoint.isDesktop` /\n135:   `viewPoint.isMobile` in the markup.\n136: - Name mobile variants consistently: `*Mobile.svelte` or `Mobile*View.svelte`,\n137:   living next to the desktop component they pair with.\n138: \n139: ## Tailwind conventions\n140: \n141: Styling is Tailwind CSS v4 utility classes, theme tokens from the runtime theme\n142: CSS, and dark-mode variants.\n143: \n144: - Use the `c-*` theme tokens for colours (`bg-c-bg`, `text-c-btn`,\n145:   `border-c-neutral-2`, `text-c-danger`, `focus:ring-c-primary`) and `s-dark-*`\n146:   tokens for dark surfaces (`dark:bg-s-dark-3`). Do not hardcode hex colours in\n147:   components.\n148: - Add `dark:` variants where the component needs different colours in dark\n149:   mode.\n150: - Class order is managed by `prettier-plugin-tailwindcss` — write classes and\n151:   let `npm run format`/the formatter sort them.\n152: - Use `size-*` utilities for component sizing (`size-6`, `size-4`) instead of\n153:   mixing `w-`/`h-` where a square is meant.\n154: - Conditional classes via the `class:` directive\n155:   (`class:pt-6={IS_DESKTOP}`) — it composes with plain `class=\"…\"`.\n156: - Utility values that repeat across the app (like the input styling on\n157:   `TextInput`) stay in the shared component, not re-pasted.\n158: \n159: ## Icons\n160: \n161: Icons come from `@lucide/svelte`, imported per-icon from\n162: `@lucide/svelte/icons/<kebab-case-name>`:\n163: \n164: ```ts\n165: import IconLoaderCircle from '@lucide/svelte/icons/loader-circle';\n166: ```\n167: \n168: ```svelte\n169: <IconLoaderCircle class=\"size-6 animate-spin text-c-btn\" />\n170: ```\n171: \n172: No hand-drawn SVGs inline, no icon-font classes; the lucide set is the icon\n173: library.\n174: \n175: ## i18n — `ts.get.*`\n176: \n177: Every user-facing string comes from the translation store:\n178: `const ts = getTranslation();` then `ts.get.layout.save`, or\n179: `ts.get.quick_add.commit_success.replace('%s', destination)`.\n180: \n181: - Never hardcode a UI string in a component. `{ts.get.layout.double_click_to_edit}`\n182:   is the pattern (`Title.svelte`).\n183: - All four locale files (`src/lib/i18n/{en,de,es,fr}.ts`) must stay in sync —\n184:   `npm run check` enforces it (`docs/AGENTS.md` hard rule).\n185: - Use `%s`/`%d` placeholders in a translation string and `.replace(...)` at the\n186:   call site when a value is interpolated.\n187: - Translation keys are typed via `src/lib/types/translation.ts`; an invalid key\n188:   is a compile error.\n189: \n190: ## Local UI state via `$state`\n191: \n192: Component-local, ephemeral state (an open modal, an edit flag, a hover box\n193: position) is a `$state` field — not a store, not a `$derived`-spam:\n194: \n195: ```ts\n196: let changeTitle = $state<boolean>(false);\n197: let titleInput = $state<HTMLInputElement | null>(null);\n198: let explanationBoxX = $state<number>(0);\n199: ```\n200: \n201: - UI-only state stays in the component; anything the route, another component\n202:   or the backend cares about belongs on a store.\n203: - `$derived` only for genuine template-read derivations\n204:   ([`BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md#derived-discipline)).\n205: \n206: ## Loading feedback\n207: \n208: Wrap store operations in the shared indicator:\n209: \n210: ```ts\n211: loadingIndicator.start();\n212: await todos.changeTitle(todo, todoTitle);\n213: loadingIndicator.stop();\n214: ```\n215: \n216: - `getLoadingIndicator()` returns the shared `LoadingIndicator` store; its\n217:   `start()`/`stop()` power the global `ui/LoadingIndicator` overlay.\n218: - Always `start()` before the await and `stop()` on every exit path. Prefer\n219:   `if (!res) return;`-style early returns with a `stop()` before them, or a\n220:   `try/finally`, so the spinner can never stay up.\n221: \n222: ## Keyboard handling via `KeyManager`\n223: \n224: Global keyboard shortcuts use the `KeyManager` store, registered per component\n225: and cleaned up in `onDestroy`. The pattern from\n226: `src/lib/components/todos/props/Title.svelte`:\n227: \n228: ```ts\n229: keyHandlers.Enter = keyManager.registerKeyDown('Enter', handleEnter);\n230: keyHandlers.Escape = keyManager.registerKeyDown('Escape', handleEscape);\n231: \n232: onDestroy(() => keyManager.unregisterAll(keyHandlers));\n233: ```\n234: \n235: - `registerKeyDown(key, handler)` returns an id; keep it in a local object so\n236:   `unregisterAll(handlers)` can release everything at once, including on blur.\n237: - Never register a handler without registering its inverse for the component's\n238:   lifetime — an orphaned global handler leaks across routes.\n239: - Plain DOM-level keys (an input's own `onkeydown`) do not need `KeyManager`;\n240:   it exists for app-wide/global shortcuts and per-edit-mode hijacks.\n241: \n242: ## Accessibility\n243: \n244: `svelte-check` is configured to ignore two a11y warnings:\n245: `a11y_click_events_have_key_events` and `a11y_no_static_element_interactions`\n246: (see the `check` script in `package.json`). That ignore is intentional, but the\n247: responsibility it waives is not: **any clickable non-native element must still\n248: be made reachable by keyboard.**\n249: \n250: - A clickable `<span>`/`<div>` needs `role=\"button\"` and `tabindex=\"0\"`, and\n251:   either an `onkeydown` doppelgänger or a `KeyManager` registration for Enter.\n252:   (`Title.svelte` uses `role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"` for its double-click\n253:   target; double-click itself has no keyboard equivalent, which is why the\n254:   accompanying hover box is not the only affordance.)\n255: - Prefer native elements (`<button>`, `<a href>`) whenever the interaction is a\n256:   real click — they get focus, keyboard and semantics for free.\n257: - Keep focus styles visible (`focus:ring-2 focus:ring-d-lightblue` on inputs,\n258:   and `focus:outline-none` only where a ring replaces the outline).\n259: \n260: ## Testability\n261: \n262: The cleanest test targets are props-driven leaves: components that take data\n263: and callbacks as props and render them (dashboard widgets, `forms/Slider`,\n264: badges/counters). They need no context seeding and are covered by\n265: `docs/TESTING.md` §4a/§8's \"Priority 2\". Components that pull stores via\n266: `getX()` but carry real logic (keyboard handling, selection, filtering UI) are\n267: testable through the context harness described in `docs/TESTING.md` §4.3.\n268: \n269: When writing a new component, favour making it easy to test: accept data via\n270: props and delegate mutations to the store either way. Render-only markup\n271: (simple icons, dividers, static labels) does not need tests and should not get\n272: them.\n273: \n274: ## Related docs\n275: \n276: - [`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) — general rules (readability,\n277:   naming, comments, `$derived`).\n278: - [`docs/STATE_SERVICES.md`](STATE_SERVICES.md) — the stores components read.\n279: - [`docs/DATA_LAYER.md`](DATA_LAYER.md) — types and i18n used in props/markup.\n280: - [`docs/TESTING.md`](TESTING.md) §4, §8 — component test strategy.\n\n(End of file - total 280 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Components\n\nPolicy for the UI layer: every `.svelte` component under\n`src/lib/components/**` and `src/routes/**`. Read\n[`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) first; this document applies the\ngeneral rules to markup and components.\n\n## Components are lean\n\nA component's job is to render state and forward user intent. All logic lives\nbelow it — in the state store or a pure service.\n\n- Read the stores a component needs **once at the top of `<script lang=\"ts\">`**,\n  never inside the markup or per-method:\n\n  ```ts\n  const todos = getTodos();\n  const loadingIndicator = getLoadingIndicator();\n  const keyManager = getKeyManager();\n  const ts = getTranslation();","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/COMPONENTS.md","text":"# Components\n\nPolicy for the UI layer: every `.svelte` component under\n`src/lib/components/**` and `src/routes/**`. Read\n[`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) first; this document applies the\ngeneral rules to markup and components.\n\n## Components are lean\n\nA component's job is to render state and forward user intent. All logic lives\nbelow it — in the state store or a pure service.\n\n- Read the stores a component needs **once at the top of `<script lang=\"ts\">`**,\n  never inside the markup or per-method:\n\n  ```ts\n  const todos = getTodos();\n  const loadingIndicator = getLoadingIndicator();\n  const keyManager = getKeyManager();\n  const ts = getTranslation();\n  ```\n\n- A component that grows a long list of `if`s and helper functions around data\n  has probably swallowed store logic: move it into a method on the store or a\n  service, then call it here. Components delegate; see\n  [`docs/STATE_SERVICES.md`](STATE_SERVICES.md).\n- Keep the `<script>` readable: store reads, `$props`, a few `$state` fields,\n  event handlers, `onDestroy`. If it stops being scannable, split components.\n\n## Type props with `$props<{...}>()`\n\nProps are typed via the runes API. There is no `export let` anywhere in this\ncodebase; do not introduce it.\n\n```ts\nlet { todo } = $props<{ todo: Todo }>();\n```\n\n```ts\nlet {\n\tinput = $bindable(),\n\tvalue = $bindable(),\n\tplaceholder,\n\tonblur,\n\tmultiLine = false,\n\theight = null,\n\ttabindex = null\n} = $props<{\n\tinput?: HTMLInputElement | HTMLTextAreaElement | null;\n\tvalue: string;\n\tplaceholder?: string;\n\tonblur?: () => void;\n\toninput?: () => void;\n\tmultiLine?: boolean;\n\theight?: number | null;\n\ttabindex?: number | null;\n}>();\n```\n\n- Use `$bindable()` only for props that the parent binds (`bind:value`); plain\n  props otherwise.\n- Event callbacks are props typed as `() => void` / `(e: Event) => void` — pass\n  them through with the `{onblur}` shorthand.\n- `let { children } = $props();` accepts the default slot fragment.\n\n## Svelte 5 syntax only\n\nNo Svelte 4 idioms. The repo has zero `on:click`, zero `createEventDispatcher`\nand zero `export let` — keep it that way.\n\n- Event attributes, not directives: `onclick`, `onkeydown`, `onblur`,\n  `onmouseover` — not `on:click`.\n- `{@render children?.()}` for the default slot, `{@render name()}` /\n  `{#snippet name()}` for named snippets.\n- Lifecycle: `onMount`, `onDestroy`, `$effect` imported from `svelte`.\n- No `createEventDispatcher`: either call a store method directly or accept an\n  event callback as a prop.\n\n## Keep markup declarative — extract conditions\n\nMarkup should read top-to-bottom: `{#if}` blocks for branching, `{#each}` for\nlists, `{value}` for output. Non-trivial conditions belong in a function or a\nnamed boolean at the top of the script, not nested inline.\n\n**Avoid** long or nested ternaries inside class attributes or other markup\nexpressions. Example of what not to write (found in\n`src/lib/components/todos/props/Title.svelte`):\n\n```svelte\nclass=\"{todos.view === 'list'\n\t? 'w-9/10'\n\t: 'w-3/4'} rounded-lg border-1 border-c-neutral-2 text-sm …\"\n```\n\nWhen a class or expression depends on more than a trivially-invertible fact,\ncompute it in the script and reference the name:\n\n```ts\nlet inputWidth = $state('w-3/4');\n// derived from todos.view in a method, or:\nfunction inputClass(): string {\n\treturn todos.view === 'list' ? 'w-9/10' : 'w-3/4';\n}\n```\n\nSame rule for `{#if}`: a `{#if}` whose condition spans several `&&`/`||` or\nrequires a nest of conditions should become a named boolean or an extracted\nrender-block function. Prefer the guard-clause style from\n[`BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md#early-returns--no-nested-short-ifs)\nwhere possible.\n\n## Prefer the shared primitives\n\nCheck `src/lib/components/ui/` (buttons, modals, badges, cards, navbars) and\n`src/lib/components/forms/` (`TextInput`, `Checkbox`, `Toggle`, `Select`,\n`Slider`, `DateInput`, …) before hand-rolling a control.\n\n- Reuse the existing primitives for inputs, modals, buttons and confirmation\n  dialogs. A hand-rolled text input with different classes than `TextInput` is\n  a smell.\n- Modal/confirm flows use the shared `Modal` primitives —\n  `ui/ConfirmationModal`, `ui/ContentModal`, `BottomSheetModal` for mobile.\n- When a primitive genuinely misses a feature, extend the shared one rather\n  than forking it per-feature.\n\n## The desktop/mobile split\n\nSeveral features keep separate view variants driven by `Viewpoint`:\n\n- `todos/views/{ListView,CardView,OverviewView,KanbanView}` and\n  `todos/TodoNavigationMobile`, `todos/views/ViewSwitcher`.\n- `calendars/views/{day,week,month,list}`, plus `views/{day,week,month}/Mobile*View`.\n- Components that switch on screen class read the store once:\n  `const viewPoint = getViewPoint();` then branch on `viewPoint.isDesktop` /\n  `viewPoint.isMobile` in the markup.\n- Name mobile variants consistently: `*Mobile.svelte` or `Mobile*View.svelte`,\n  living next to the desktop component they pair with.\n\n## Tailwind conventions\n\nStyling is Tailwind CSS v4 utility classes, theme tokens from the runtime theme\nCSS, and dark-mode variants.\n\n- Use the `c-*` theme tokens for colours (`bg-c-bg`, `text-c-btn`,\n  `border-c-neutral-2`, `text-c-danger`, `focus:ring-c-primary`) and `s-dark-*`\n  tokens for dark surfaces (`dark:bg-s-dark-3`). Do not hardcode hex colours in\n  components.\n- Add `dark:` variants where the component needs different colours in dark\n  mode.\n- Class order is managed by `prettier-plugin-tailwindcss` — write classes and\n  let `npm run format`/the formatter sort them.\n- Use `size-*` utilities for component sizing (`size-6`, `size-4`) instead of\n  mixing `w-`/`h-` where a square is meant.\n- Conditional classes via the `class:` directive\n  (`class:pt-6={IS_DESKTOP}`) — it composes with plain `class=\"…\"`.\n- Utility values that repeat across the app (like the input styling on\n  `TextInput`) stay in the shared component, not re-pasted.\n\n## Icons\n\nIcons come from `@lucide/svelte`, imported per-icon from\n`@lucide/svelte/icons/<kebab-case-name>`:\n\n```ts\nimport IconLoaderCircle from '@lucide/svelte/icons/loader-circle';\n```\n\n```svelte\n<IconLoaderCircle class=\"size-6 animate-spin text-c-btn\" />\n```\n\nNo hand-drawn SVGs inline, no icon-font classes; the lucide set is the icon\nlibrary.\n\n## i18n — `ts.get.*`\n\nEvery user-facing string comes from the translation store:\n`const ts = getTranslation();` then `ts.get.layout.save`, or\n`ts.get.quick_add.commit_success.replace('%s', destination)`.\n\n- Never hardcode a UI string in a component. `{ts.get.layout.double_click_to_edit}`\n  is the pattern (`Title.svelte`).\n- All four locale files (`src/lib/i18n/{en,de,es,fr}.ts`) must stay in sync —\n  `npm run check` enforces it (`docs/AGENTS.md` hard rule).\n- Use `%s`/`%d` placeholders in a translation string and `.replace(...)` at the\n  call site when a value is interpolated.\n- Translation keys are typed via `src/lib/types/translation.ts`; an invalid key\n  is a compile error.\n\n## Local UI state via `$state`\n\nComponent-local, ephemeral state (an open modal, an edit flag, a hover box\nposition) is a `$state` field — not a store, not a `$derived`-spam:\n\n```ts\nlet changeTitle = $state<boolean>(false);\nlet titleInput = $state<HTMLInputElement | null>(null);\nlet explanationBoxX = $state<number>(0);\n```\n\n- UI-only state stays in the component; anything the route, another component\n  or the backend cares about belongs on a store.\n- `$derived` only for genuine template-read derivations\n  ([`BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md#derived-discipline)).\n\n## Loading feedback\n\nWrap store operations in the shared indicator:\n\n```ts\nloadingIndicator.start();\nawait todos.changeTitle(todo, todoTitle);\nloadingIndicator.stop();\n```\n\n- `getLoadingIndicator()` returns the shared `LoadingIndicator` store; its\n  `start()`/`stop()` power the global `ui/LoadingIndicator` overlay.\n- Always `start()` before the await and `stop()` on every exit path. Prefer\n  `if (!res) return;`-style early returns with a `stop()` before them, or a\n  `try/finally`, so the spinner can never stay up.\n\n## Keyboard handling via `KeyManager`\n\nGlobal keyboard shortcuts use the `KeyManager` store, registered per component\nand cleaned up in `onDestroy`. The pattern from\n`src/lib/components/todos/props/Title.svelte`:\n\n```ts\nkeyHandlers.Enter = keyManager.registerKeyDown('Enter', handleEnter);\nkeyHandlers.Escape = keyManager.registerKeyDown('Escape', handleEscape);\n\nonDestroy(() => keyManager.unregisterAll(keyHandlers));\n```\n\n- `registerKeyDown(key, handler)` returns an id; keep it in a local object so\n  `unregisterAll(handlers)` can release everything at once, including on blur.\n- Never register a handler without registering its inverse for the component's\n  lifetime — an orphaned global handler leaks across routes.\n- Plain DOM-level keys (an input's own `onkeydown`) do not need `KeyManager`;\n  it exists for app-wide/global shortcuts and per-edit-mode hijacks.\n\n## Accessibility\n\n`svelte-check` is configured to ignore two a11y warnings:\n`a11y_click_events_have_key_events` and `a11y_no_static_element_interactions`\n(see the `check` script in `package.json`). That ignore is intentional, but the\nresponsibility it waives is not: **any clickable non-native element must still\nbe made reachable by keyboard.**\n\n- A clickable `<span>`/`<div>` needs `role=\"button\"` and `tabindex=\"0\"`, and\n  either an `onkeydown` doppelgänger or a `KeyManager` registration for Enter.\n  (`Title.svelte` uses `role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"` for its double-click\n  target; double-click itself has no keyboard equivalent, which is why the\n  accompanying hover box is not the only affordance.)\n- Prefer native elements (`<button>`, `<a href>`) whenever the interaction is a\n  real click — they get focus, keyboard and semantics for free.\n- Keep focus styles visible (`focus:ring-2 focus:ring-d-lightblue` on inputs,\n  and `focus:outline-none` only where a ring replaces the outline).\n\n## Testability\n\nThe cleanest test targets are props-driven leaves: components that take data\nand callbacks as props and render them (dashboard widgets, `forms/Slider`,\nbadges/counters). They need no context seeding and are covered by\n`docs/TESTING.md` §4a/§8's \"Priority 2\". Components that pull stores via\n`getX()` but carry real logic (keyboard handling, selection, filtering UI) are\ntestable through the context harness described in `docs/TESTING.md` §4.3.\n\nWhen writing a new component, favour making it easy to test: accept data via\nprops and delegate mutations to the store either way. Render-only markup\n(simple icons, dividers, static labels) does not need tests and should not get\nthem.\n\n## Related docs\n\n- [`docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`](BEST_PRACTICES.md) — general rules (readability,\n  naming, comments, `$derived`).\n- [`docs/STATE_SERVICES.md`](STATE_SERVICES.md) — the stores components read.\n- [`docs/DATA_LAYER.md`](DATA_LAYER.md) — types and i18n used in props/markup.\n- [`docs/TESTING.md`](TESTING.md) §4, §8 — component test strategy.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":280,"totalLines":280,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/COMPONENTS.md","time":{"start":1791709463108,"end":1791709463174}},"id":"prt_12a34c212001E08ZZCBjomKL2N","sessionID":"ses_ed5cc28c2fferyTpyy2Zhxl0sU","messageID":"msg_12a34b5e1001ZNrJUcqI77qOdJ"}}
